{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SriC936wmfM7ESQX3JAgxU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D19 seen, D20+ forecast)\n2\t\n3\tScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\n4\tGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 19 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\n5\tTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\n6\talways in `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\n7\treflection). D15\n8\tadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\n9\tMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\n10\tlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\n11\tD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n12\t`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\n13\tD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\n14\tkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n15\tD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\n16\tgenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\n17\tclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\n18\tSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\n19\tThe risk for D20+ is the **answer leaving the puzzle JSON** (computed by the native export / dex, nested dex, encrypted)\n20\tmore than the theme. D15-D19 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation +\n21\tdecoys -> string encryption -> reflection): next expect control-flow flattening / switch dispatchers / opaque predicates,\n22\tdynamic proxies / MethodHandles / invoke-custom, dynamic code loading, a tiny custom bytecode VM, anti-tamper (signature,\n23\tchecksum), root/emulator/debugger/Frida detection, and SEVERAL `ANS-` candidates where only the one reaching `proof=`\n24\tcounts. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection) and old ones recur (d18 xor): any\n25\tunknown codec must be decodable from `ANS-` alone -- and first check whether `data` already IS the answer (d15, d19).\n26\t\n27\tTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\n28\tapksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\n29\tandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\n30\thbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\n31\ttshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\n32\tMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\n33\tabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\n34\tTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\n35\tno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors 