proof_flow_scan` [i] | high |\n121\t| 79 | Control-flow flattening / switch dispatcher state machine | gap | value assembled across `while(true){switch(state)}` cases | one huge method with `packed-switch` in a loop, a state int reassigned in every case | `jadx` (shows the loop); emulate with `dex_eval_scan` [i] if it supports switch + loops | high: next RESILIENCE step |\n122\t| 80 | Dynamic proxy / MethodHandle / invoke-custom / lambdas | gap | target method behind `Proxy.newProxyInstance` InvocationHandler or `MethodHandles.Lookup.findStatic` | `java/lang/reflect/Proxy`, `InvocationHandler`, `MethodHandles$Lookup`, `invoke-polymorphic`/`invoke-custom` (dex 038+), `LambdaMetafactory` | `jadx`; androguard opcodes 0xfa-0xfd | med-high: \"dispatch\" without `forName` |\n123\t| 81 | Custom bytecode VM (virtualised method) | gap | byte-array program run by an in-dex interpreter; output = answer | `[B` program const + loop with `packed-switch` on `program[pc]`, `pc` increments | `jadx`; reimplement the opcode table in py / run it in `dex_eval_scan` | med |\n124\t| 82 | JNI reflection callback (native `FindClass`/`GetStaticMethodID`/`CallStaticObjectMethod` into Java) | gap | Java method named by `.rodata` strings in the `.so`, called from native | `.so` strings like `com/huntress/...`, `(Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/String;`; imports via JNIEnv vtable offsets | `strings -a f.so`; `rizin -A`; resolve the named Java method in the dex | med: merges native + reflection tracks |\n125\t\n126\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n127\t\n128\t```\n129\t0. Always first: python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"   # puzzle->zip->dex->apktool/jadx\n130\t   If it prints ANS-... and the prompt is the usual \"backend answer code\": submit. Do NOT chase 127.0.0.1:19090.\n131\t1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n132\t   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      puzzle codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n133\t                                    int list beside data (D17 `indexed`, D5 `split`): r[order[i]] = data[i]; else gather\n134\t   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n135\t                                    Java_*_native*(int) + *_accepts helper (D16 gate): objdump -d it; the value it returns\n136\t                                    is the answer (D16: &arena_value = the .rodata ANS- literal; bypass len 65536)\n137\t   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n138\t   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n139\t   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n140\t   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n141\t   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n142\t   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading: unzip it, jadx it, re-run extract_answer on it\n143\t   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n144\t   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n145\t   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n146\t   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n147\t   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n148\t   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n149\t   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n150\t   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n151\t2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n152\t   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n153\t   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n154\t3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n155\t   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n156\t   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). droidasc getmanifest x.apk prints the XML.\n157\t4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n158\t   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader -> asset dex     SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher/IvParameterSpec -> static key decrypt\n159\t   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n160\t   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n161\t   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n162\t   su/magisk/RootBeer/goldfish/frida/TracerPid -> flag sits in the gated branch: read it, never run it\n163\t   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> reflection_scan     BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n164\t   Proxy/InvocationHandler/MethodHandles/invoke-custom -> resolve the real target; packed-switch in a loop -> flattened CFG\n165\t   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n166\t5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n167\t   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n168\t   String decryptors (D18 TT `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte`): dex_eval_scan, else jadx the helper, take the ARGS from\n169\t   each call site, re-implement in py; unknown key/rolling scheme -> solve it from the ANS- known plaintext.\n170\t   R8/decoys (D17): hint strings like \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" name the chain; >1 ANS- candidate -> keep\n171\t   the one appended before `proof=` in ChallengeActivity, never the first regex hit. Reflection/dispatch (D19 theme):\n172\t   names may be encoded or picked by a key from the deep link/asset; evaluate only the invoked target, not its twins.\n173\t   lib scanners for code-side answers (not in extract_answer): renamed_chain_scan, proof_flow_scan, dex_eval_scan,\n174\t   reflection_scan, mapping_restore_scan, signing_block_scan, zip_structure_scan  (all lib.android, take apk path)\n175\t6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n176\t7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n177\t8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3 or 5).\n178\t```\n179\t\n180\t## Readiness gaps\n181\t\n182\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n183\t`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\n184\tutf16-string-pool-scan, nested-container-recurse, dex-native-split-assembly, static-key-cipher-decode,\n185\tdecode-any-chain-peel, native-so-emulate-export, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, asset-db-prefs-backup,\n186\tidentity-derived-key, hermes-hbc-string-table, cert-and-signing-facts, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\n187\tjni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, registernatives-table, native-stack-string, multi-abi-arm-native,\n188\tdex-native-call-args, native-gated-branch-read, dex-gated-branch-consts, webview-asset-js-scan,\n189\tcert-pin-and-nsc-facts, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\n190\tdalvik-mini-interpreter, permutation-transposition-family, reflection-name-resolve, proguard-mapping-restore,\n191\tapk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-scan, integrity-derived-key, ans-prefix-numeric-compose,\n192\tcustom-alphabet-decode, asset-cipher-dex-loader, native-init-array-decrypt, resource-id-const-resolve,\n193\tmessagedigest-derived-answer, v1-manifest-digest-verify, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, aab-proto-manifest-parse,\n194\trolling-xor-keystream-family, decrypt-call-site-args-eval, known-string-obfuscator-signatures,\n195\tidentifier-collision-resolve, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, java-serialized-object-parse, jwt-token-decode-verify,\n196\tprotobuf-asset-wire-decode, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt.\n197\t\n198\t```json\n199\t[\n200\t  {\"id\": \"dispatch-key-resolve\", \"concept\": \"reflective dispatch tables keyed by a runtime string (row 77; D19 TT `dispatch`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19's TT dex added `dispatch` with no reflection code yet; the code-side version picks a handler by key. Pure python over the dex (androguard or the mini interpreter): recover key -> target maps from (a) `HashMap.put(const-string, Method|Class|lambda|const-string class name)` in <clinit>/<init>, (b) Java string-switch (`String.hashCode()` -> sparse-switch -> `equals(const)` -> case block), (c) arrays of class-name strings indexed by an int. Resolve the KEY the app actually supplies: deep-link path segment / `getQueryParameter` name from the manifest intent-filter (scheme/host/pathPrefix), manifest meta-data, puzzle JSON fields (`route`, `key`, `entry`, `dispatch`), const-strings passed at the call site. Run only the selected target via dex_eval_scan/reflection_scan and return its ANS- value first, other targets as demoted candidates.\"},\n201\t  {\"id\": \"entry-reachable-callgraph-rank\", \"concept\": \"generated equivalent call graphs: N look-alike classes, one wired (row 78)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 prompt: 'reconstruct reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs'. Build a dex call graph from ChallengeActivity/MainActivity onCreate (and the manifest's launch/deep-link activities) including reflective edges (forName/getDeclaredMethod names resolved by reflection_scan, const-class, Proxy targets) and virtual dispatch to concrete subclasses. Group structurally equivalent methods (same opcode sequence modulo constants/names) and report, per group, which member is reachable from the entry and which value reaches `proof=`. Feed as a strong rank signal to proof_flow_scan; unreachable twins with ANS- literals are decoys.\"},\n202\t  {\"id\": \"flattened-cfg-switch-eval\", \"concept\": \"control-flow flattening / while(true)-switch(state) dispatchers (row 79)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next RESILIENCE step after reflection. Ensure the dex mini interpreter executes packed-switch/sparse-switch, backward gotos and int state updates with a step budget (~200k insns), so a flattened method that appends answer chars across cases (StringBuilder / char[] writes) runs to completion; when the state seed comes from a param, try the const at each call site. Also a static unflattener fallback: from the dispatcher's state transitions (each case ends with const state; goto head) recover the case order from the initial state and concatenate the const-strings/chars in that order. Regex the output for ANS-.\"},\n203\t  {\"id\": \"proxy-methodhandle-invokecustom\", \"concept\": \"dynamic proxies, MethodHandles, invoke-polymorphic/invoke-custom, lambdas (row 80)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Dispatch' without Class.forName: extend reflection resolution to java.lang.reflect.Proxy.newProxyInstance(handler) -> route interface calls into InvocationHandler.invoke with the Method name const; MethodHandles.Lookup.findStatic/findVirtual/findGetter(Class, name, MethodType) -> resolve target by name + descriptor; dex 038+ invoke-custom call sites (call_site_ids -> bootstrap LambdaMetafactory -> implementation method handle) and invoke-polymorphic MethodHandle.invoke/invokeExact; Kotlin/D8 desugared lambdas (`-$$Lambda$`/`$ExternalSyntheticLambda` classes) -> their single target method. Pure python dex parsing (call_site_ids/method_handles sections) + dex_eval_scan.\"},\n204\t  {\"id\": \"clean-device-env-stubs\", \"concept\": \"root/emulator/debugger/Frida checks gating the answer, evaluated as a clean device (rows 41, 47, 48, 66)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"MASVS-RESILIENCE detection days are the obvious remainder of the arc. Give dex_eval_scan a 'clean physical device' environment model: File.exists/canRead on su/magisk/busybox/frida paths -> false, Build.TAGS -> 'release-keys', Build.FINGERPRINT/MODEL/HARDWARE/PRODUCT -> a Pixel profile (not goldfish/ranchu/sdk/generic), Debug.isDebuggerConnected/waitingForDebugger -> false, ApplicationInfo.flags FLAG_DEBUGGABLE clear, System.getProperty('ro.kernel.qemu') -> null, /proc/self/status TracerPid 0, /proc/self/maps without frida/xposed, Socket connect 27042 -> refused, PackageManager.getPackageInfo(magisk/xposed pkgs) -> NameNotFound. Run each method whose body references those APIs/strings and report the ANS- value on the clean path.\"},\n205\t  {\"id\": \"tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret\", \"concept\": \"virtualised method: custom bytecode program + in-dex interpreter (row 81)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Detect a method with a [B/[I program (fill-array-data or base64/hex const) and a loop dispatching on program[pc] via packed-switch. First try running it in dex_eval_scan with the step budget; else lift: map each case to an op (push const, xor, add, sub, rot, load/store reg, emit char, jump) by pattern-matching its Dalvik ops, then interpret the program in python. Output candidates to the ANS regex.\"},\n206\t  {\"id\": \"jni-reflection-callback\", \"concept\": \"native code calling back into Java by name (FindClass/GetStaticMethodID) (row 82)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Merges the D15-D16 native track with D19 reflection. In each .so: collect .rodata strings shaped like JNI class paths (`com/huntress/...`, `java/lang/...`) and method descriptors `(...)L...;`, pair them by proximity/xref (capstone over the Java_* / JNI_OnLoad bodies: lea of string -> call via JNIEnv vtable offsets FindClass 0x30, GetStaticMethodID 0x388, CallStaticObjectMethod 0x390, GetMethodID 0x108, NewStringUTF 0x538), resolve the named Java method in the dex and run it with dex_eval_scan; also return NewStringUTF literal args. x86_64 + arm64.\"},\n207\t  {\"id\": \"kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines\", \"concept\": \"Kotlin @Metadata original names + coroutine state machines\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If the fixture moves to Kotlin: decode `kotlin/Metadata` annotations (d1 = protobuf-encoded strings with the JvmProtoBuf string table, d2 = original names) to restore class/function names after R8; and evaluate `invokeSuspend` state machines (switch on `label` field, values carried in `L$0`/`I$0` spill fields) by running the cases in label order. Strings to the ANS regex; names to renamed_chain/reflection resolution.\"},\n208\t  {\"id\": \"dex-bytecode-integrity-gate\", \"concept\": \"anti-tamper: answer keyed by dex checksum/signature of classes.dex or a method's own bytes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"integrity-derived-key covers APK/cert digests; add the in-dex variants: app reads its own classes.dex (getPackageCodePath + ZipFile) and computes Adler32/CRC32/SHA-1/MD5 over the whole dex, the header checksum field, or a code_item byte range, then xors/hashes it into the answer. Compute every such digest from the shipped bytes (dex header adler32 @0x08, sha1 @0x0c, zip CRC of classes.dex) and try them as keys against puzzle data / dex arrays with the ANS- known plaintext.\"},\n209\t  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n210\t  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n211\t  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n212\t  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n213\t  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n214\t  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n215\t  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n216\t  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n217\t  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"},\n218\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"}\n219\t]\n220\t```\n221\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b5ec962-bca7-4255-ac86-7981bea3612b","uuid":"eaba8df0-98df-4e73-ab43-e7e28c2b0066","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:15:16.708Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md","content":"# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D19 seen, D20+ forecast)\n\nScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\nGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 19 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\nTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\nalways in `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\nreflection). D15\nadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\nMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\nlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\nD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\nD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\nkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\ngenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\nclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\nSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\nThe risk for D20+ is the **answer leaving the puzzle JSON** (computed by the native export / dex, nested dex, encrypted)\nmore than the theme. D15-D19 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation +\ndecoys -> string encryption -> reflection): next expect control-flow flattening / switch dispatchers / opaque predicates,\ndynamic proxies / MethodHandles / invoke-custom, dynamic code loading, a tiny custom bytecode VM, anti-tamper (signature,\nchecksum), root/emulator/debugger/Frida detection, and SEVERAL `ANS-` candidates where only the one reaching `proof=`\ncounts. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection) and old ones recur (d18 xor): any\nunknown codec must be decodable from `ANS-` alone -- and first check whether `data` already IS the answer (d15, d19).\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\nLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n\n| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D19+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n| 2 | Exported Service / AIDL / Messenger | gap | `onBind`/`onStartCommand`/`handleMessage` compares + returns secret | `<service exported>`, `extends Binder`, `$Stub`, `IInterface`, `Messenger` | `jadx -d out x.apk` [i]; `droidasc findrefs x.apk type Landroid/os/Binder;` | med: next IPC theme |\n| 3 | Broadcast receiver (exported, dynamic, ordered/sticky) | gap | `onReceive` action/extra check; action strings in dex | `<receiver exported>`, `registerReceiver`, `sendOrderedBroadcast`, custom `ACTION_*` | `aapt dump xmltree ...`; `jadx` grep `onReceive` | med-high: classic unused IPC theme |\n| 4 | Content provider (SQLi, path traversal, FileProvider paths) | seen D6 | puzzle; real: `query()` / `openFile()`, `res/xml/*paths*.xml` | `<provider exported grantUriPermissions>`, `UriMatcher`, `<root-path>`, `../` | `apktool d -f -o out x.apk` [i]; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/file_paths.xml` | med (mixed Mastery) |\n| 5 | Custom permission weakness (normal level, typo, missing) | gap | manifest | `<permission protectionLevel=\"normal\">`, `android:permission` on comp vs `uses-permission` | `aapt dump permissions x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 6 | Task hijacking / StrandHogg | gap | manifest attrs (answer = static) | `taskAffinity`, `allowTaskReparenting=\"true\"`, `launchMode=\"singleTask\"` | `aapt dump xmltree ... \\| grep -E 'taskAffinity\\|launchMode\\|Reparent'` | med |\n| 7 | Tapjacking / overlay | gap | layout XML or manifest | `filterTouchesWhenObscured`, `FLAG_WINDOW_IS_OBSCURED`, `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` | `apktool d` then `grep -r filterTouches out/res` | med |\n| 8 | Deep link (custom scheme, param parsing) | seen D2 | puzzle; real: `getQueryParameter` branch | `<data android:scheme=..>`, `getData()`, `getQueryParameter` | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme>` [i]; `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 9 | App Links / autoVerify / assetlinks | gap | host + cert SHA-256 (assetlinks needs the signing fp) | `android:autoVerify=\"true\"`, `https` scheme+host | `apksigner verify --print-certs x.apk` [i]; `keytool -printcert -jarfile x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 10 | Intent redirection / nested Intent / `Intent.parseUri` | seen D3 | puzzle; real: forwarded Intent reaches a private comp | `getParcelableExtra(..Intent)`, `startActivity(`, `parseUri`, `intent://` | `jadx`; `droidasc findrefs x.apk method parseUri` | high (mixed) |\n| 11 | PendingIntent (mutable / implicit base) | seen D4 | puzzle | `FLAG_MUTABLE`, `PendingIntent.getActivity` with empty Intent | `strings -a classes.dex \\| grep -i pendingintent` | high (mixed) |\n| 12 | Fragment injection (PreferenceActivity) | gap | `isValidFragment` returns true | `PreferenceActivity`, `:android:show_fragment` | `jadx` | low |\n| 13 | WebView JS interface | seen D7 | puzzle; real: `@JavascriptInterface` getter returns secret | `addJavascriptInterface`, `@JavascriptInterface` | `jadx`; `droidasc findrefs x.apk method addJavascriptInterface` | high (mixed) |\n| 14 | WebView file access / UXSS / loadUrl from extra | gap | `assets/*.html`/`*.js` holding the secret, or the URL itself | `setAllowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs(true)`, `file:///android_asset/`, `loadUrl(getIntent()` | `unzip -l x.apk 'assets/*'`; `unzip -p x.apk 'assets/*.html'` | med-high |\n| 15 | WebView URL-allowlist bypass (`shouldOverrideUrlLoading`) | gap | allowlist check strings | `startsWith(\"https://`, `endsWith(`, `getHost()`, `loadDataWithBaseURL` | `jadx` | med |\n| 16 | allowBackup / adb backup `.ab` | seen D5 | puzzle; real: `*.ab` -> tar -> `sp/*.xml`/`db/*.db` | `allowBackup=\"true\"`, `fullBackupContent`, `dataExtractionRules`, header `ANDROID BACKUP` | `dd if=b.ab bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` [i]; abe [M] | med |\n| 17 | SharedPreferences secrets | seen D11 | puzzle; real: `shared_prefs/*.xml` or dex default value | `getSharedPreferences`, `MODE_WORLD_READABLE`, `EncryptedSharedPreferences` | `unzip -l`; `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 18 | SQLite / Room / Realm | seen D12 | puzzle; real: `assets/*.db` row, `rawQuery` | `SQLiteOpenHelper`, `rawQuery`, magic `SQLite format 3\\0`, `.realm` | `sqlite3 f.db .dump` [i] | med |\n| 19 | External storage / world-readable files | gap | path constant + file in assets | `getExternalStorageDirectory`, `requestLegacyExternalStorage`, `MODE_WORLD_*` | `jadx` grep | med |\n| 20 | Logcat leakage | gap | `Log.d(tag, secret)` constant in dex | `Landroid/util/Log;`, tag strings near secret | `strings -a classes*.dex`; `jadx` grep `Log\\.` | med |\n| 21 | Clipboard / screenshot / keyboard cache | gap | n/a (fact question) | `ClipboardManager`, `FLAG_SECURE`, `textNoSuggestions` | `jadx`, `apktool d` | low-med |\n| 22 | Hardcoded secret in strings.xml / BuildConfig | gap | `resources.arsc` string, `BuildConfig` static field | `resources.arsc` present, `BuildConfig` class, `api_key`/`secret` res names | `aapt dump --values resources x.apk \\| grep -B2 ANS-` [i]; `apktool d` + `grep -r ANS- out/res`; `jadx` `BuildConfig.java` | high: cheapest escalation |\n| 23 | Firebase / google-services misconfig | gap | `firebase_database_url`, `google_api_key` res or `google-services.json` | `firebaseio.com`, `AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}`, `google_app_id` | `apktool d` + grep; offline (answer = the key/URL or a JSON in assets) | med |\n| 24 | Cloud/API keys (AWS, Stripe, JWT, OAuth) | gap | dex/arsc constants | `AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}`, `sk_live_`, `eyJ` | `strings -a` + regex; apkleaks [M] | med |\n| 25 | Cleartext traffic | seen D8 | puzzle | `usesCleartextTraffic=\"true\"`, `http://` URLs | `aapt dump xmltree` | high (mixed) |\n| 26 | Permissive TrustManager / HostnameVerifier | seen D9 | puzzle | `X509TrustManager`, empty `checkServerTrusted`, `ALLOW_ALL_HOSTNAME_VERIFIER` | `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 27 | Network Security Config | seen D10 | puzzle; NSC itself (domain/pin values) | `networkSecurityConfig`, `cleartextTrafficPermitted`, `<certificates src=\"user\">` | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml` [i] | high (mixed) |\n| 28 | Certificate pinning (OkHttp / NSC pin-set) | gap | pin `sha256/<b64>` constants; pinned host | `CertificatePinner`, `<pin-set>`, `sha256/` | `jadx`; frida [M] (no device: static only) | med-high: follows D8-D10 |\n| 29 | Bundled keystore / cert with hardcoded password | gap | `res/raw/*.bks\\|*.p12\\|*.pem`, password in dex | `KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"\\|\"PKCS12\")`, `.load(..,\"pw\".toCharArray())` | `keytool -list -v -keystore f.p12 -storepass PW` [i]; `openssl pkcs12 -in f.p12 -nodes -passin pass:PW` [i] | med |\n| 30 | Shipped traffic capture (pcap/HAR) | gap (d8 prompt hinted, none shipped) | HTTP body/header | `*.pcap`, `*.har` entries | `tshark -r f.pcap -Y http -T fields -e http.file_data` [i] | low |\n| 31 | Keystore misuse | seen D13 | puzzle | `AndroidKeyStore`, `KeyGenParameterSpec`, no `setUserAuthenticationRequired` | `jadx` | med (mixed) |\n| 32 | Predictable RNG / nonce / seed | seen D14 | puzzle; real: `new Random(seed)` -> regenerate in py | `java/util/Random`, `setSeed`, `currentTimeMillis` | `jadx`; reimplement LCG `(x*0x5DEECE66D+0xB) mod 2^48` | med (mixed) |\n| 33 | Static AES key/IV, ECB, `SecretKeySpec` | gap | ciphertext in asset/JSON + key/IV dex strings | `SecretKeySpec`, `AES/ECB/PKCS5Padding`, `IvParameterSpec`, 16/24/32-char constants | `jadx`; py `Crypto.Cipher.AES` [i] | high: the obvious \"real crypto\" codec |\n| 34 | Weak hash / KDF / short PIN | gap | hash constant -> brute force | `MessageDigest.getInstance(\"MD5\"\\|\"SHA-1\")`, `PBKDF2WithHmacSHA1`, low iter