{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RrbYPxjaYVtP47VjhULThJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/mobile-android.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b5ec962-bca7-4255-ac86-7981bea3612b","uuid":"a70f6d20-c96b-4509-bb07-22cc7a38d6e8","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:18:09.433Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/mobile-android.md","content":"# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-20; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture: `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`, `classes.dex`,\n  `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF` (6 entries). Extras: d10 `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` +\n  `resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, ~12.8 KB); d20 `assets/payload.dex` (508 B\n  plain `dex\\n035`, 7 entries, APK 12768 B). One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16 uppercase hex.\n- Each day has a new Android IPC/security THEME, written in the manifest `<meta-data android:name=\"huntress.mechanic\">`\n  and in a dex string `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable\n  PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider, JS-interface origin trust, cleartext session, permissive X509\n  trust manager, NSC exception, SharedPreferences credential, client-side SQLite authz, app-controlled Keystore key,\n  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` d15, `jni_length` d16, `identifier_obfuscation` d17, `string_decryption` d18,\n  `reflective_dispatch` d19, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\" d20). The theme was mostly flavour: theme stub classes\n  (`WebViewBridge`, `TrustEveryone`, `NativeLibrarySecrets`, `JNIBoundary`, `EncryptedStrings`, `ReflectionMaze`,\n  `LoadedLater`) were never needed, and prompts demanding a live action were still static. d16 had the first REAL gate in\n  code (TT JNI export). **d20 was the first day the answer was NOT in the puzzle JSON**: `data` pointed at a second dex.\n- What varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split, hex,\n  caesar+key, then repeats; d15-d16 `native` and d19 `reflection` = theme-named, `data` already the plaintext; d17\n  `indexed` = permutation; d18 back to `xor`; d20 `dynamic` = `data` is a ZIP ENTRY PATH (`assets/payload.dex`) and the\n  answer is a const-string inside that entry). Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day: check\n  `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name in the APK, then decode from the first 4 chars, which must become `ANS-`.\n- **Since d15 Mastery is a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets are APKs from earlier days plus one of today's (d15: 01/07/10/\n  14/15; d16: 01/04/11/13/16; d17: 04/08/12/14/17; d18: 03/07/12/13/18; d19: 03/05/11/18/19; d20: d02 reverse, d09\n  base64, d11 xor, d18 xor, d20 dynamic), all under today's prompt text. Solve each set from its own APK.\n- In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?\n  case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM\n  accepted the statically recovered value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 20 days.\n- Pattern d16-d20: the SINGLE variant carries only flavour; the TT build carries the real mechanic as dex strings (d16 JNI\n  gate, d17 `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy`, d18 `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`, d19 `dispatch` +\n  `STRUCTURAL`, d20 `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` + `STRUCTURAL` -- an\n  `entry:class` pointer, still no `DexClassLoader` API anywhere). Read the TT/Mastery APK's dex strings, not just the single's.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44,41,232, d16\n  Mastery d04-set 21, d17 d04-set 104, d18: 20/99/233/100, d19 d18-set 44 -- full 0-255 range, never assume printable;\n  caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4/5/15, d14: 9/10/17,4,7,14) and split/offset parameters re-roll per variant: read them from\n  `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs (`reverse`, `base64`, `native`, `reflection`) differ only in `data`.\n  d17 `indexed`: `order[]` was the SAME list in every variant (`order[i] = (3 + 7*i) mod 20`), only `data` changed.\n  d20 `dynamic`: `data` = `assets/payload.dex` in single, TT and the Mastery d20 set (same 508 B payload layout, only the\n  `ANS-` literal changed). Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`; if `data` names a zip\n  entry, read that entry and run the whole candidate chain on its bytes; else `decode_any`; unknown name -> known-\n  plaintext `ANS-` trick; any int-list field of len(data) -> try scatter and gather, keep the regex match.\n- **Answer indirection (NEW d20)** -- the JSON value stopped being the answer: it named the entry that holds it. Inside\n  `payload.dex` (class `com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`, strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:<mechanic>`)\n  the only `ANS-` literal was the answer. TT/Mastery host dex also named the class (`<entry>:<dotted class>`) and a method\n  `moduleContract`. Rule: follow the pointer; if the payload ever holds >1 candidate, take the value of the field/method\n  the host names (`ANSWER`, `moduleContract`), not the first regex hit; if the entry is not a valid dex/zip, unwrap it by\n  magic known plaintext (`dex\\n0`, `PK\\x03\\x04`, `\\x7fELF`) before giving up.\n- **Mastery set mix (d15+)** -- sets are fixtures of DIFFERENT days (codec, theme, package `dNN`, extra entries like\n  `res/xml/...`, `lib/x86_64/*.so` or `assets/payload.dex`); the puzzle JSON `day` field and dex `DAY-NN:` tag name the\n  source day. The day picks re-roll per attempt (the pre-start `status` preview lists different MOB-NN than the dealt\n  sets); the last set was always today's, with its own manifest label (cosmetic). d16: the QUESTION's case ref/package did\n  NOT match the APK's own. Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding -- never branch on the day or case ref.\n- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref `MOB-NN-<10 hex>`, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback\n  attempt slug change per variant. None of these feed the answer.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. 3 sets (d1-d7, d10-d14) or 5\n  (d8, d9, d15-d20). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume a count.\n- **Dex decoy/hint strings (d17-d20)** -- single dex: `CODEC`, `CONTROL`, `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>` tag, `describe`; TT\n  and today's Mastery set: NO `DAY-NN` tag and no `describe`, instead the mechanic as strings (sizes single -> TT: d17\n  2588 -> 2672 B, d18 2588 -> 2628, d19 2596 -> 2656, d20 2564 -> 2636). Rule: never require `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` to find or\n  decode the puzzle; a TT-only string (`decryptByte`, `dispatch`, `moduleContract`) is the cue to the next escalation.\n- **Answer location** -- the puzzle JSON d1-d19 (d15-d16 also in `.so` `.rodata`); d20 a nested asset dex named by the\n  JSON. Fallback chain: `raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`, `extract_answer`.\n- **Native lib shape (d16)** -- single shipped the 13648 B d15-style lib (no `loadLibrary`); TT/Mastery a 14128 B lib with\n  `huntress_arena_length_accepts` + `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence`. Rule: never key on export names or lib size.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json`. triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` and prints the JSON |\n| puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (table below). Check the result fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before you submit |\n| `data` is a path (`assets/payload.dex`, codec `dynamic`, d20) | `unzip -p x.apk assets/payload.dex \\| strings -a \\| grep ANS-` (d20: plain const in class `...payload.Module`). Not a dex magic -> known-plaintext unwrap, then recurse |\n| extra `assets/*.dex\\|*.jar\\|*.zip\\|*.bin` (d20) | secondary-code-loading theme: inspect it like `classes.dex`; host strings `<entry>:<class>` + `moduleContract` name the target |\n| int list next to `data` (d17 `indexed`, d5 `split`) | `order[i]` is the OUTPUT slot of `data[i]`: `r[order[i]] = data[i]`. Tell: `A`,`N`,`S`,`-` sit where `order` has 0..3 |\n| Codec name not in the table (d7 `caesar`, d15 `native`, d17 `indexed`, d19 `reflection`, d20 `dynamic`) | `data` already `ANS-`? (d15, d19). An entry name? (d20). Else `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key |\n| `lib/<abi>/*.so` (d15-d16 `libarena.so`, ~14 KB, not stripped) | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-`, `nm -D --defined-only`; only if no literal, route to binary-re (the `Java_*` export) |\n| Native GATE (d16 `Java_*_nativeEvidence(int)` -> `*_length_accepts`) | the gate only decides whether the `.rodata` literal is returned. Bypass input if ever asked: `objdump -d` the checker (d16: 65536) |\n| No puzzle JSON, or nothing decodes to `ANS-` | `lib.android.extract_answer` (zip scan, dex strings incl. multidex, apktool/jadx), then `strings -a classes*.dex assets/* lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |\n| Need theme, component, scheme, exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk`; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`; `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |\n| 1-letter classes, hint \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\", `decoy` (d17) | asset first. If the answer leaves it: `jadx --deobf`, follow the chain the hint names; prefer the value that flows into `proof=` |\n| `EncryptedStrings`/`decryptByte` (d18), `ReflectionMaze`/`dispatch` (d19) | asset first. Code-side: `dex_eval_scan` / `reflection_scan`, then `proof_flow_scan` to pick the value that reaches `proof=` |\n| Handler logic (URL, extras, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |\n| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it: device-local. The answer is static |\n| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session\" d8, \"exploit a CA\" d9, \"challenge-signed\" d20) | still static: `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/extra dex first. d20's \"signed\" module had no verify code; the v1 `MANIFEST.MF` merely lists its digest |\n| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen) | 24-byte header + zlib: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` |\n| Mastery `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact`). Ids `setN.answer`; each set may be another day's fixture |\n\nPuzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):\n- `plain`, `native` (d15-d16, duplicated in the `.so`), `reflection` (d19): `data` is the answer.\n- `dynamic` (d20): `data` = zip entry path; read the entry, `ANS-` literal inside the dex (`puzzle_candidates` yields the\n  path string itself, so the solver's `raw_entry_scan` fallback found it -- follow the pointer explicitly).\n- `reverse`; `base64` (d3, d9, d13); `hex` (d6, d12).\n- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`, `chr(ord(c) - key)` over EVERY char (digits and `-` too, `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`);\n  a letters-only ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.\n- `xor` (d4, d11, d18): base64 data, XOR every byte with int `key` (0-255).\n- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, `order[i]` = OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]`. Try both readings, keep the `ANS-` one.\n- `indexed` (d17): 20 chars + `order[20]`, `r[order[i]] = data[i]` (`permutation_candidates` tries scatter + gather).\n- `lib.android.decode_payload` / `puzzle_candidates(apk)` / `decode_any` (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`) cover these.\n  Code-side scanners (call yourself; not in `extract_answer`): `renamed_chain_scan`, `proof_flow_scan`, `dex_eval_scan`,\n  `reflection_scan`, `mapping_restore_scan`, `signing_block_scan`, `zip_structure_scan`, `integrity_key_scan`.\n\n## Day by day\n\n**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (~5.4 min, ~4 min lost probing\n`127.0.0.1:19090`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay\n`xor` (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot (27 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (~3 min, 2.3 min lost on\nthe loopback).\n\n**Days 7-15** (theme stubs never needed; 0 wrong, TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window): d7 WebView Bridge new `caesar`; d8\nCleartext Session `reverse`; d9 Trust Everyone `base64`; d10 Network Config Split `split` (8-entry + NSC); d11 Local\nSecrets `xor`; d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`; d14 Predictable Crypto `caesar` (json-load the\n`\\\\`/`<` escapes). d15 Native Library Secrets: first `libarena.so` (answer literal in `.rodata`), codec `native` =\nplaintext; first MIXED-DAY Mastery.\n\n**Days 16-19** (asset held the answer; 0 wrong; carried-over solver CORRECT in ~2-25 s): d16 JNI Boundary, `native`; TT\n`.so` added the `nativeEvidence(int)` gate (65536). d17 Name Collapse, NEW `indexed` (race probe silent, duel worker added\nthe decoder -> ~24.5 s); TT hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c`. d18 Encrypted Strings, `xor` (3rd time); TT\n`decryptByte`. d19 Reflection Maze, NEW `reflection` = plaintext; no reflection API in any dex; TT `dispatch`.\n\n**Day 20 — Loaded Later** (manifest `huntress.mechanic`=`secondary DEX loading`, dex `DAY-20:dynamic_dex:secondary DEX\nloading`, class `LoadedLater`, deep link `huntress20://loaded-later/unlock`; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary\nDEX and recover the module contract.\")\n- Artifact: 7-entry APK (12768 B): the usual fixture + `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain `dex\\n035`, listed with a\n  SHA-256 in the v1 `MANIFEST.MF` like every entry). Puzzle `{\"codec\":\"dynamic\",\"data\":\"assets/payload.dex\"}` -- a\n  POINTER. The payload dex = one class `com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` with strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`,\n  `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:secondary DEX loading` and the `ANS-` literal. Host dex had no `DexClassLoader`/`loadClass`/\n  signature/digest code in any variant: \"challenge-signed\" and \"module contract\" were narrative.\n- TT + today's Mastery set: host dex 2636 B, `DAY-20` tag dropped, adds `STRUCTURAL`, `moduleContract` and\n  `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (entry:class pointer). Payload unchanged in shape.\n- Key insight: first day the answer LEFT the JSON value; it sat one hop away, still as a plain literal. `strings -a` on\n  the extracted payload (triage pre-extracts `assets/`) showed it in one command. The carried-over solver's `answer()`\n  returned nothing (`puzzle_candidates` yields the path string), the `raw_entry_scan` fallback found the literal.\n- Time: race probe CORRECT (probe 1.74 s, ~8.4 s after server start 13:00:09.98Z -> 13:00:18.34Z), no LLM turn needed.\n  TT in-window 3.06 s (solve 0.99 s); Mastery 5 sets (d02 reverse, d09 base64, d11 xor key 41, d18 xor key 100, d20\n  dynamic) in-window 5.19 s (solve 0.53 s). Timed runs reported `no_clock: true` (window null, as on d19). All first\n  try, 0 wrong. GM spelling: same `answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 or 5 sets), one APK per set.\n- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding, no whitespace.\n- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-20). The GM accepts the statically recovered\n  value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend answer code\".\n- Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An\n  empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.\n- Prompt boilerplate: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In Mastery the text is\n  today's and the case ref may not match the APK (d16). Neither was ever needed for the answer.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: ~4 min (d1), ~30 s (d4), ~2.3 min (d6).\n  `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If a static value matches the answer_format, submit it.\n- **Taking `data` at face value** (d20): `data` was an entry path, not a value. Never submit or \"decode\" a string that\n  names a zip entry; open the entry. Always fullmatch the ANS regex on the final value.\n- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15+): sets come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.\n- **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15-d16): the `.so` is ~14 KB, unstripped, the answer a literal. Use\n  `strings`/`nm`, then `objdump -d` of the one `Java_*` export. Same for d20's payload: `strings` before `jadx`.\n- **Trusting the question's case ref in Mastery** (d16): it can name a different day/case than the APK it points at.\n- **New codec, generic solver silent** (d17 `indexed`, ~20 s lost): when the JSON has an unknown codec, write the\n  5-line decoder straight away (anchor on `ANS-`); do not wait on lib or decompile anything.\n- **Trusting dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` strings** (d17-d20 TT): the TT dex drops the tag. Key the decoder on the JSON's fields.\n- **split/indexed order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate against the answer regex instead of guessing.\n- **caesar codec:** shift over raw codepoints, not the alphabet; json-load (escapes `<`/`>`), never regex the raw text.\n- **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.\n- **Short timed windows** are dominated by start + download + submit; solve is <1 s. No decompiling in-window: the\n  solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess.\n- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove\n  server-side impact\", d15 \"split configuration\", d16 \"type or length assumption\", d18 \"strings that reach\n  security-sensitive APIs\", d19 \"reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs\", d20 \"challenge-signed\n  secondary DEX ... module contract\"): judge by what the APK contains (extra entries, `Random`/`Cipher`/`forName`/\n  `DexClassLoader`/`MessageDigest` refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.\n- **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json`; check `hctf status` before re-solving.\n- **Escalation watch:** d20 moved the answer one hop (JSON -> nested dex). Next cheap steps: the payload encrypted /\n  XOR'd / zipped (unwrap by magic known plaintext, key from host dex), several payloads where only the one whose digest\n  matches a pinned hash (\"challenge-signed\") is loaded, >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host naming the real field/\n  method (`moduleContract`), class shadowing between host and payload, or a stage-2 loader. If several candidates\n  appear, take the one the code actually returns into `proof=` (`proof_flow_scan`), never the first regex hit.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":218,"newStart":1,"newLines":178,"lines":["-# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)","+# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-20; updated after every day)"," "," How the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a","   guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field."," - Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture: `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`, `classes.dex`,","   `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF` (6 entries). Extras: d10 `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` +","-  `resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, ~12.8 KB). One question, `answer` = `ANS-` +","-  16 uppercase hex.","+  `resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, ~12.8 KB); d20 `assets/payload.dex` (508 B","+  plain `dex\\n035`, 7 entries, APK 12768 B). One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16 uppercase hex."," - Each day has a new Android IPC/security THEME, written in the manifest `<meta-data android:name=\"huntress.mechanic\">`","   and in a dex string `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable","   PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider, JS-interface origin trust, cleartext session, permissive X509","   trust manager, NSC exception, SharedPreferences credential, client-side SQLite authz, app-controlled Keystore key,","-  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` \"challenge-owned JNI shared library\" d15, `jni_length` \"Java-to-native validation","-  mismatch\" d16, `identifier_obfuscation` \"R8-style identifier collapse\" d17, `string_decryption` \"runtime string","-  decryption\" d18, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\" d19). The theme was flavour only: no day required","-  exploiting it, even with a matching stub class (`WebViewBridge`, `TrustEveryone`, `PredictableCrypto`,","-  `NativeLibrarySecrets`, `JNIBoundary`, `EncryptedStrings`, `ReflectionMaze`) or a prompt demanding a live action. d16 is the first day whose TT/Mastery build had a REAL gate in code (a JNI export guarding the answer),","-  yet the answer was still a literal in the asset and in `.rodata`.","+  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` d15, `jni_length` d16, `identifier_obfuscation` d17, `string_decryption` d18,","+  `reflective_dispatch` d19, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\" d20). The theme was mostly flavour: theme stub classes","+  (`WebViewBridge`, `TrustEveryone`, `NativeLibrarySecrets`, `JNIBoundary`, `EncryptedStrings`, `ReflectionMaze`,","+  `LoadedLater`) were never needed, and prompts demanding a live action were still static. d16 had the first REAL gate in","+  code (TT JNI export). **d20 was the first day the answer was NOT in the puzzle JSON**: `data` pointed at a second dex."," - What varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split, hex,","-  caesar+key, then repeats; d15-d16 `native`, whose `data` is already the plaintext answer; d17 `indexed` = permutation","-  `data` + `order[]`; d18 back to `xor`, its 3rd day after d4/d11 -- old codecs recur on new themes; d19 `reflection`,","-  a theme-named codec whose `data` is already the plaintext, like `native`). The dex also holds","-  the codec name next to a `CODEC` string constant. Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day:","-  decode it from the first 4 chars, which must become `ANS-`.","-- **Since d15 Mastery is a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets are APKs from earlier days plus one of today's (d15: d01 plain,","-  d07 caesar, d10 split, d14 caesar, d15 native; d16: d01 plain, d04 xor, d11 xor, d13 base64, d16 native; d17: d04 xor,","-  d08 reverse, d12 hex, d14 caesar, d17 indexed; d18: d03 base64, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d18 xor; d19: d03","-  base64, d05 split, d11 xor, d18 xor, d19 reflection), all under","-  today's prompt text. Solve each set from its own puzzle JSON, never from \"today's codec\".","+  caesar+key, then repeats; d15-d16 `native` and d19 `reflection` = theme-named, `data` already the plaintext; d17","+  `indexed` = permutation; d18 back to `xor`; d20 `dynamic` = `data` is a ZIP ENTRY PATH (`assets/payload.dex`) and the","+  answer is a const-string inside that entry). Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day: check","+  `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name in the APK, then decode from the first 4 chars, which must become `ANS-`.","+- **Since d15 Mastery is a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets are APKs from earlier days plus one of today's (d15: 01/07/10/","+  14/15; d16: 01/04/11/13/16; d17: 04/08/12/14/17; d18: 03/07/12/13/18; d19: 03/05/11/18/19; d20: d02 reverse, d09","+  base64, d11 xor, d18 xor, d20 dynamic), all under today's prompt text. Solve each set from its own APK."," - In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?","   case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM","-  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 19 days.","-- Escalation watch: d15 shipped the first native lib and d16 the first native GATE (`Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence","-  (env, cls, int len)` returns `arena_value` only if `huntress_arena_length_accepts(len, 0)`: `len > 0xffff &&","-  (uint16)len == 0`, i.e. 65536). The answer was STILL in the asset and in `.rodata`. If a later day drops it from the","-  asset, read the gate statically and take the value it returns (`lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain).","-- Pattern d16-d19: the SINGLE variant carries only flavour; the TT build carries the real mechanic in code (d16 JNI gate,","-  d17 renamed class `a` + dex hint `R8-style collapse: follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy`/`telemetry` strings,","-  d18 a `decryptByte` method + `STRUCTURAL` string in class `EncryptedStrings`, d19 only `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings","-  -- no `forName`/`getMethod`/`invoke` anywhere). Every time the asset STILL held the answer.","-  Read the TT/Mastery APK's dex strings when you reverse a day, not just the single's.","+  accepted the statically recovered value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 20 days.","+- Pattern d16-d20: the SINGLE variant carries only flavour; the TT build carries the real mechanic as dex strings (d16 JNI","+  gate, d17 `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy`, d18 `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`, d19 `dispatch` +","+  `STRUCTURAL`, d20 `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` + `STRUCTURAL` -- an","+  `entry:class` pointer, still no `DexClassLoader` API anywhere). Read the TT/Mastery APK's dex strings, not just the single's."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)","-- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44, d16 Mastery","-  d04-set 21, d11-set 232, d17 d04-set 104, d18: 20/99/233, d19 Mastery d11-set 109, d18-set 44 -- full 0-255 range, so never assume printable keys; caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4, d14: 9/10/17,4,7, d15 Mastery d07-set 15, d14-set 4) and split/offset parameters re-roll per variant:","-  read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs (`reverse`, `base64`, `native`, `reflection`) differ","-  only in `data`. Theme-named codecs (`native` d15-d16, `reflection` d19) carried the PLAINTEXT in `data` in every variant.","-  d17 `indexed`: `order[]` was the SAME list in single, TT and the Mastery d17 set (`order[i] = (3 + 7*i) mod 20`), only","-  `data` changed -- still read it from the JSON, a later day may re-roll it.","-  Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`, else `decode_any`; unknown name -> known-plaintext","-  `ANS-` trick; any int-list field of len(data) -> try scatter and gather, keep the regex match.","-- **Mastery set mix (NEW d15)** -- sets can be fixtures of DIFFERENT days (codec, theme, package `dNN`, extra entries","-  like `res/xml/...` or `lib/x86_64/*.so` all differ per set; the puzzle JSON `day` field and dex `DAY-NN:` tag name the","-  source day). The day picks re-roll per attempt (d15: 01/07/10/14/15 vs 03/07/09/13/15; d16: 01/04/11/13/16; d17:","-  04/08/12/14/17, while the pre-start `status` preview listed MOB-02/06/09 -- re-dealt at start; d18: preview MOB-01/06/","-  10/15/18, dealt 03/07/12/13/18; d19: 03/05/11/18/19, d05 split as a 6-entry APK, `order` [2,0,1]); the last set was","-  always today's. Today's Mastery set has its own manifest label","-  (`Day 18 Mastery | concept Day 18: Encrypted Strings`, manifest 3540 B vs 3492 B) -- cosmetic. d16: the QUESTION's case ref/package (`MOB-06-..`, `d08`, `d14`) did NOT match the APK's own","-  (`MOB-04`, `d11`, `d13`), so the contract text does not predict the codec either.","-  Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding (`puzzle_candidates` over each APK) -- never branch on the day or case ref.","+- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44,41,232, d16","+  Mastery d04-set 21, d17 d04-set 104, d18: 20/99/233/100, d19 d18-set 44 -- full 0-255 range, never assume printable;","+  caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4/5/15, d14: 9/10/17,4,7,14) and split/offset parameters re-roll per variant: read them from","+  `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs (`reverse`, `base64`, `native`, `reflection`) differ only in `data`.","+  d17 `indexed`: `order[]` was the SAME list in every variant (`order[i] = (3 + 7*i) mod 20`), only `data` changed.","+  d20 `dynamic`: `data` = `assets/payload.dex` in single, TT and the Mastery d20 set (same 508 B payload layout, only the","+  `ANS-` literal changed). Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`; if `data` names a zip","+  entry, read that entry and run the whole candidate chain on its bytes; else `decode_any`; unknown name -> known-","+  plaintext `ANS-` trick; any int-list field of len(data) -> try scatter and gather, keep the regex match.","+- **Answer indirection (NEW d20)** -- the JSON value stopped being the answer: it named the entry that holds it. Inside","+  `payload.dex` (class `com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`, strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:<mechanic>`)","+  the only `ANS-` literal was the answer. TT/Mastery host dex also named the class (`<entry>:<dotted class>`) and a method","+  `moduleContract`. Rule: follow the pointer; if the payload ever holds >1 candidate, take the value of the field/method","+  the host names (`ANSWER`, `moduleContract`), not the first regex hit; if the entry is not a valid dex/zip, unwrap it by","+  magic known plaintext (`dex\\n0`, `PK\\x03\\x04`, `\\x7fELF`) before giving up.","+- **Mastery set mix (d15+)** -- sets are fixtures of DIFFERENT days (codec, theme, package `dNN`, extra entries like","+  `res/xml/...`, `lib/x86_64/*.so` or `assets/payload.dex`); the puzzle JSON `day` field and dex `DAY-NN:` tag name the","+  source day. The day picks re-roll per attempt (the pre-start `status` preview lists different MOB-NN than the dealt","+  sets); the last set was always today's, with its own manifest label (cosmetic). d16: the QUESTION's case ref/package did","+  NOT match the APK's own. Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding -- never branch on the day or case ref."," - **Per-variant identity** -- case ref `MOB-NN-<10 hex>`, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback","   attempt slug change per variant. None of these feed the answer.","-- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. Set count varies: 3 sets","-  (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets (d8, d9, d15, d16). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3.","-- **Dex decoy/hint strings (d17-d18)** -- single dex: `CODEC`, `CONTROL`, `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>` tag, `describe`; TT","-  and today's Mastery set: NO `DAY-NN` tag and no `describe`, instead the mechanic in code -- d17 `R8-style collapse:","-  follow b -> a and ignore field c`, `decoy`, `telemetry`, `authorization` (2672 B vs 2588 B); d18 `decryptByte`,","-  `STRUCTURAL`, the mechanic name as a bare string (2628 B vs 2588 B); d19 `dispatch`, `STRUCTURAL`, the mechanic string,","-  `CODEC` kept (2656 B vs 2596 B), still no reflection API. Rule: never require the dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN`","-  strings to find or decode the puzzle; a TT-only method name (`decryptByte`) is the cue to what the next escalation","-  computes in code.","-- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON (d15-d16: also duplicated in the `.so` `.rodata`); if it decodes","-  to nothing, fall back to dex/resources/native (`raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`).","-- **Native lib shape (NEW d16)** -- same day, different `.so` builds: the single variant shipped the d15-style 13648 B lib","-  (exports `huntress_arena_secret`/`huntress_arena_day` only, dex 2584 B, no `loadLibrary`); TT and the Mastery d16 set","-  shipped a 14128 B lib adding `huntress_arena_length_accepts` + `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence` (dex 2760 B with","-  `System.loadLibrary(\"arena\")`, `nativeEvidence`, and a description string \"Java int length narrows to an unsigned","-  native 16-bit boundary before authorization\"). Rule: never key on export names or lib size; take the asset value,","-  cross-check `ANS-` literals in the `.so`; if none, follow the `Java_*` export to the pointer it returns.","+- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. 3 sets (d1-d7, d10-d14) or 5","+  (d8, d9, d15-d20). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume a count.","+- **Dex decoy/hint strings (d17-d20)** -- single dex: `CODEC`, `CONTROL`, `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>` tag, `describe`; TT","+  and today's Mastery set: NO `DAY-NN` tag and no `describe`, instead the mechanic as strings (sizes single -> TT: d17","+  2588 -> 2672 B, d18 2588 -> 2628, d19 2596 -> 2656, d20 2564 -> 2636). Rule: never require `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` to find or","+  decode the puzzle; a TT-only string (`decryptByte`, `dispatch`, `moduleContract`) is the cue to the next escalation.","+- **Answer location** -- the puzzle JSON d1-d19 (d15-d16 also in `.so` `.rodata`); d20 a nested asset dex named by the","+  JSON. Fallback chain: `raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`, `extract_answer`.","+- **Native lib shape (d16)** -- single shipped the 13648 B d15-style lib (no `loadLibrary`); TT/Mastery a 14128 B lib with","+  `huntress_arena_length_accepts` + `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence`. Rule: never key on export names or lib size."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," "," | You see | First move |"," |---|---|","-| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (held the answer all 19 days). triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` and prints the JSON |","+| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json`. triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` and prints the JSON |"," | puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (table below). Check the result fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before you submit |","-| puzzle JSON with an int list next to `data` (d17 `indexed`: `data` 20 chars + `order[20]`) | `order[i]` is the OUTPUT slot of `data[i]` (scatter, same as `split`): `r[order[i]] = data[i]`. Tell: `data` holds `A`,`N`,`S`,`-` at the positions where `order` has 0,1,2,3 |","-| Codec name not in the table (d7 `caesar`, d15 `native`, d17 `indexed`, d19 `reflection`) | first check whether `data` already matches `ANS-` (d15, d19: a codec named after the theme was plaintext). Else compare `data[:4]` with `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key |","-| `lib/<abi>/*.so` in the APK (d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`, 13.6-14.1 KB, not stripped) | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` and `nm -D --defined-only` first (d15: exports `huntress_arena_secret`/`huntress_arena_day`, 0x20-byte `.text`, answer as a literal in `.rodata`). Only if the answer is not a literal, route to binary-re (rizin / pyelftools + capstone, or the JNI `Java_*` export) |","-| Native GATE (d16: `Java_*_nativeEvidence(int)` -> `*_length_accepts`; \"type or length assumption\") | the gate only decides whether the export returns `arena_value`; that pointer is the `.rodata` `ANS-` literal. If a question ever asks for the bypass input: `objdump -d --no-show-raw-insn f.so` the checker (d16: `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -> 65536) |","-| \"Recover split configuration from DEX and a native library\" (d15) | the \"split\" was narrative: the asset `data` and the `.so` string were the SAME full answer, and the dex held only `CODEC`/`native`/`CONTROL`. Cross-check the two, submit |","-| No puzzle JSON, or it decodes to no `ANS-` | `lib.android.extract_answer` (zip scan, then dex strings incl. multidex, then apktool/jadx scan), then `strings -a classes*.dex lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |","-| Need the theme, component, scheme or exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` (fast). `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`. Also `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |","-| 1-letter classes `<pkg>/a`, `b`; dex hint \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\", strings `decoy`/`telemetry` (d17 R8 theme) | first check the asset (it still held the answer d17). If the answer ever leaves it: `jadx --deobf -d w/jadx x.apk`, follow the chain the hint names, ignore the named decoy field; prefer the value that flows into `proof=` |","-| String-encryption theme: class `EncryptedStrings`, dex method `decryptByte`, mechanic `runtime string decryption` (d18) | asset first (d18: `xor` codec, answer there). If the answer ever leaves it: `lib.android.dex_eval_scan` (mini Dalvik evaluator; note it feeds params `\"\"`/0, so a helper called with constant args needs those args from the call site) and `jadx` the helper; re-implement the per-byte loop in python, anchor on `ANS-` |","-| Reflection theme: class `ReflectionMaze`, mechanic `reflective secret dispatch`, TT strings `dispatch`/`STRUCTURAL` (d19) | asset first (d19: answer in `data`). If it ever leaves: `lib.android.reflection_scan(apk)` (runs the methods that call `getDeclaredMethod`/`Field.get`, resolving encoded names), then `proof_flow_scan` to pick the value that reaches `proof=` |","-| Need handler logic (URL built, extras read, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, then `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; whole app: `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |","-| Need resources or strings.xml / smali | `apktool d -f -o work/apktool x.apk` |","-| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it. It is device-local (refused on Homebase, times out elsewhere). The answer is static |","-| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session against the backend\" d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9) | still static: check `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/network config first; none shipped. Decode the asset, submit |","-| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen yet) | Android backup = 24-byte header + zlib stream: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` (or abe.jar) |","-| Mastery artifact names like `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the `delivery N: ` prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact` does this). Ids are `setN.answer`; each set may be a different day's fixture (d15) |","+| `data` is a path (`assets/payload.dex`, codec `dynamic`, d20) | `unzip -p x.apk assets/payload.dex \\| strings -a \\| grep ANS-` (d20: plain const in class `...payload.Module`). Not a dex magic -> known-plaintext unwrap, then recurse |","+| extra `assets/*.dex\\|*.jar\\|*.zip\\|*.bin` (d20) | secondary-code-loading theme: inspect it like `classes.dex`; host strings `<entry>:<class>` + `moduleContract` name the target |","+| int list next to `data` (d17 `indexed`, d5 `split`) | `order[i]` is the OUTPUT slot of `data[i]`: `r[order[i]] = data[i]`. Tell: `A`,`N`,`S`,`-` sit where `order` has 0..3 |","+| Codec name not in the table (d7 `caesar`, d15 `native`, d17 `indexed`, d19 `reflection`, d20 `dynamic`) | `data` already `ANS-`? (d15, d19). An entry name? (d20). Else `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key |","+| `lib/<abi>/*.so` (d15-d16 `libarena.so`, ~14 KB, not stripped) | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-`, `nm -D --defined-only`; only if no literal, route to binary-re (the `Java_*` export) |","+| Native GATE (d16 `Java_*_nativeEvidence(int)` -> `*_length_accepts`) | the gate only decides whether the `.rodata` literal is returned. Bypass input if ever asked: `objdump -d` the checker (d16: 65536) |","+| No puzzle JSON, or nothing decodes to `ANS-` | `lib.android.extract_answer` (zip scan, dex strings incl. multidex, apktool/jadx), then `strings -a classes*.dex assets/* lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |","+| Need theme, component, scheme, exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk`; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`; `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |","+| 1-letter classes, hint \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\", `decoy` (d17) | asset first. If the answer leaves it: `jadx --deobf`, follow the chain the hint names; prefer the value that flows into `proof=` |","+| `EncryptedStrings`/`decryptByte` (d18), `ReflectionMaze`/`dispatch` (d19) | asset first. Code-side: `dex_eval_scan` / `reflection_scan`, then `proof_flow_scan` to pick the value that reaches `proof=` |","+| Handler logic (URL, extras, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |","+| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it: device-local. The answer is static |","+| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session\" d8, \"exploit a CA\" d9, \"challenge-signed\" d20) | still static: `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/extra dex first. d20's \"signed\" module had no verify code; the v1 `MANIFEST.MF` merely lists its digest |","+| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen) | 24-byte header + zlib: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` |","+| Mastery `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact`). Ids `setN.answer`; each set may be another day's fixture |"," "," Puzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):","-- `plain`: data is the answer. `native` (d15-d16): same, duplicated in `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`. `reflection` (d19): same.","-- `reverse`: reverse the string (`...-SNA` -> `ANS-...`).","-- `base64` (d3, d9, d13): `base64 -d` (`QU5TLTNEM0I4MDM5NTI0MEI4RUU=` -> `ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`).","-- `hex` (d6, d12): `xxd -r -p`.","-- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`. Plain ASCII codepoint shift: `chr(ord(c) - key)` for EVERY char (digits and `-`","-  shift too, e.g. `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`). A letters-only mod-26 ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.","-- `xor` (d4, d11, d18): data is base64. b64-decode, then XOR every byte with the int `key` (0-255, re-rolled per variant;","-  lib also accepts a numeric-string or repeating string key).","-- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, where `order[i]` is the OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]` (not `parts[order[i]]`).","-  Try both readings and keep the one that fullmatches `ANS-`.","-- `indexed` (d17): `{data: 20 chars, order: [20 ints]}`, per-CHARACTER permutation with the same semantics:","-  `r[order[i]] = data[i]` (`-2FE1A2D163AA1N51SC0` + `[3,10,17,4,...]` -> `ANS-E26A5C21D3110FA1`). Built into lib after","-  d17: `lib.android.permutation_candidates(p)` tries scatter + gather over ANY int-list field of len(data) (also","-  `perm*`/`shuffle*`/unknown codecs), and `transposition_candidates(s)` covers keyless stride/rail-fence shuffles.","-- `lib.android.decode_payload` covers every codec above, `puzzle_candidates(apk)` also does split/indexed (both order readings),","-  and `decode_any` is the name-agnostic fallback (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`). Call them instead of re-typing a","-  table. Unknown codec + int key: `key_or_shift = f(data[:4], \"ANS-\")` (xor: byte ^; shift: ord diff).","-- Code-side scanners prebuilt after d17 (for when the answer leaves the asset): `renamed_chain_scan` (follow R8 `b -> a`","-  chains, hint-aware), `proof_flow_scan` (rank `ANS-` candidates by what reaches `proof=`), `dex_eval_scan` (mini Dalvik","-  evaluator for xor/char-array builders), `reflection_scan`, `mapping_restore_scan`, `signing_block_scan`,","-  `zip_structure_scan`, `integrity_key_scan`. `extract_answer(apk)` chains only the entry/dex/nested/cipher/cert/integrity","-  stages -- call the chain/proof/eval/reflection scanners yourself.","+- `plain`, `native` (d15-d16, duplicated in the `.so`), `reflection` (d19): `data` is the answer.","+- `dynamic` (d20): `data` = zip entry path; read the entry, `ANS-` literal inside the dex (`puzzle_candidates` yields the","+  path string itself, so the solver's `raw_entry_scan` fallback found it -- follow the pointer explicitly).","+- `reverse`; `base64` (d3, d9, d13); `hex` (d6, d12).","+- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`, `chr(ord(c) - key)` over EVERY char (digits and `-` too, `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`);","+  a letters-only ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.","+- `xor` (d4, d11, d18): base64 data, XOR every byte with int `key` (0-255).","+- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, `order[i]` = OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]`. Try both readings, keep the `ANS-` one.","+- `indexed` (d17): 20 chars + `order[20]`, `r[order[i]] = data[i]` (`permutation_candidates` tries scatter + gather).","+- `lib.android.decode_payload` / `puzzle_candidates(apk)` / `decode_any` (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`) cover these.","+  Code-side scanners (call yourself; not in `extract_answer`): `renamed_chain_scan`, `proof_flow_scan`, `dex_eval_scan`,","+  `reflection_scan`, `mapping_restore_scan`, `signing_block_scan`, `zip_structure_scan`, `integrity_key_scan`."," "," ## Day by day"," ","-**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, one codec per day, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (CORRECT ~5.4 min,","-~4 min lost probing `127.0.0.1:19090` via `hctf hb exec curl`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s; Mastery expired 8x","-in a 6 s window until Homebase prewarm); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay `xor` key per","-variant 103/189/31/81 (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot of `parts[i]` (27 s; TT/Mastery 7 s","-window, solve 0.08 s of 5.3 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (exported provider with a null `query()` stub; ~3 min, 2.3 min","-lost on the loopback).","+**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (~5.4 min, ~4 min lost probing","+`127.0.0.1:19090`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay","+`xor` (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot (27 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (~3 min, 2.3 min lost on","+the loopback)."," ","-**Days 7-15** (same fixture; theme stubs never needed; all 0 wrong, TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window): d7 WebView Bridge,","-new `caesar` key 10, spotted by eye (`K`-10=`A`), 52 s; d8 Cleartext Session `reverse` (no traffic shipped); d9 Trust","-Everyone `base64`; d10 Network Config Split `split` (8-entry fixture + NSC, still static); d11 Local Secrets `xor` key 81","-(dex `client_secret` a decoy); d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`; d14 Predictable Crypto","-`caesar` key 9 (raw JSON escapes `\\\\`/`<` -- json-load it). d12+ solved in ~3-5 s by the carried-over solver. d15 Native","-Library Secrets (`jni_secret`): first `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13648 B, answer literal in `.rodata`), codec `native` =","-plaintext answer = the `.so` string (\"split\" was narrative). First MIXED-DAY Mastery (d01/07/10/14/15).","+**Days 7-15** (theme stubs never needed; 0 wrong, TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window): d7 WebView Bridge new `caesar`; d8","+Cleartext Session `reverse`; d9 Trust Everyone `base64`; d10 Network Config Split `split` (8-entry + NSC); d11 Local","+Secrets `xor`; d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`; d14 Predictable Crypto `caesar` (json-load the","+`\\\\`/`<` escapes). d15 Native Library Secrets: first `libarena.so` (answer literal in `.rodata`), codec `native` =","+plaintext; first MIXED-DAY Mastery."," ","-**Days 16-18** (fixture unchanged; asset held the answer every time; 0 wrong): d16 JNI Boundary (`jni_length`), codec","-`native`; TT/Mastery `.so` added `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int len)` -> `huntress_arena_length_accepts`","-(`len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` = 65536) returning the `.rodata` literal; probe ~7 s, TT 5.3 s, Mastery 5.5 s. d17 Name","-Collapse (`identifier_obfuscation`): renamed class `<pkg>/a`, NEW codec `indexed` (`r[order[i]] = data[i]`, same `order` in","-all variants); TT dex hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy`/`telemetry`. Race probe FAILED (no decoder), duel","-worker added `_indexed` -> CORRECT ~24.5 s. d18 Encrypted Strings (`string_decryption`): codec `xor` (3rd time, b64 + int","-key); single dex had no cipher code, TT/Mastery added `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`; carried-over solver","-CORRECT ~5.2 s after start, TT 2.42 s, Mastery 5.05 s in-window. Lesson: the title names the theme; the codec decides.","+**Days 16-19** (asset held the answer; 0 wrong; carried-over solver CORRECT in ~2-25 s): d16 JNI Boundary, `native`; TT","+`.so` added the `nativeEvidence(int)` gate (65536). d17 Name Collapse, NEW `indexed` (race probe silent, duel worker added","+the decoder -> ~24.5 s); TT hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c`. d18 Encrypted Strings, `xor` (3rd time); TT","+`decryptByte`. d19 Reflection Maze, NEW `reflection` = plaintext; no reflection API in any dex; TT `dispatch`."," ","-**Day 19 — Reflection Maze** (manifest `huntress.mechanic`=`reflective secret dispatch`, dex","-`DAY-19:reflective_dispatch:reflective secret dispatch`, class `ReflectionMaze`, deep link `huntress19://reflection-maze/","-unlock`; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs.\"; dex blurb \"cross the","-reflective secret dispatch boundary\")","-- Artifact: the 6-entry fixture (APK 12704 B, dex 2596 B, no `.so`/arsc); classes `MainActivity`, `ChallengeActivity`,","-  `ReflectionMaze`. NEW codec name `reflection`, but `{\"codec\":\"reflection\",\"data\":\"ANS-<16 hex>\"}` -- `data` was already","-  the answer (same shape as `native`). No dex in any variant held `forName`/`getDeclaredMethod`/`invoke`: there was no","-  reflective dispatch to reconstruct and no \"equivalent call graphs\" -- one class, one value.","-- TT + today's Mastery set: dex 2656 B, `DAY-19` tag and `describe` dropped, `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` added (`CODEC`","-  kept). Same TT-only-hint pattern as d17-d18, still unused for the answer.","-- Key insight / tools: none needed beyond the carried-over solver: `puzzle_candidates` returns `data` when it already","-  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`, whatever the codec name. Unknown codec name -> regex-check `data` before decoding.","-- Time: race probe submitted from the solver -> CORRECT 1.9 s probe, ~3.2 s after start (13:00:07.3Z -> 13:00:10.5Z), no","-  LLM turn. TT in-window 1.88 s (solve 0.2 s); Mastery 5 sets (d03 base64, d05 split, d11 xor, d18 xor, d19 reflection)","-  in-window 1.34 s (solve 0.06 s). All first try, 0 wrong. GM spelling: same `answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`.","+**Day 20 — Loaded Later** (manifest `huntress.mechanic`=`secondary DEX loading`, dex `DAY-20:dynamic_dex:secondary DEX","+loading`, class `LoadedLater`, deep link `huntress20://loaded-later/unlock`; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary","+DEX and recover the module contract.\")","+- Artifact: 7-entry APK (12768 B): the usual fixture + `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain `dex\\n035`, listed with a","+  SHA-256 in the v1 `MANIFEST.MF` like every entry). Puzzle `{\"codec\":\"dynamic\",\"data\":\"assets/payload.dex\"}` -- a","+  POINTER. The payload dex = one class `com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` with strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`,","+  `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:secondary DEX loading` and the `ANS-` literal. Host dex had no `DexClassLoader`/`loadClass`/","+  signature/digest code in any variant: \"challenge-signed\" and \"module contract\" were narrative.","+- TT + today's Mastery set: host dex 2636 B, `DAY-20` tag dropped, adds `STRUCTURAL`, `moduleContract` and","+  `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (entry:class pointer). Payload unchanged in shape.","+- Key insight: first day the answer LEFT the JSON value; it sat one hop away, still as a plain literal. `strings -a` on","+  the extracted payload (triage pre-extracts `assets/`) showed it in one command. The carried-over solver's `answer()`","+  returned nothing (`puzzle_candidates` yields the path string), the `raw_entry_scan` fallback found the literal.","+- Time: race probe CORRECT (probe 1.74 s, ~8.4 s after server start 13:00:09.98Z -> 13:00:18.34Z), no LLM turn needed.","+  TT in-window 3.06 s (solve 0.99 s); Mastery 5 sets (d02 reverse, d09 base64, d11 xor key 41, d18 xor key 100, d20","+  dynamic) in-window 5.19 s (solve 0.53 s). Timed runs reported `no_clock: true` (window null, as on d19). All first","+  try, 0 wrong. GM spelling: same `answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 or 5 sets), one APK per set."," - Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding, no whitespace.","-- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-19). The GM accepts the decoded","-  `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend","-  answer code returned for this case\".","+- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-20). The GM accepts the statically recovered","+  value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend answer code\"."," - Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An","   empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.","-- Prompt boilerplate repeats daily: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In a mixed","-  Mastery bundle the prompt text is today's; on d15 each set's `NN` named its source day, but on d16 the question's case","-  ref/package did not match the APK's own (MOB-06 question -> a d04 APK). Neither was ever needed for the answer.","+- Prompt boilerplate: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In Mastery the text is","+  today's and the case ref may not match the APK (d16). Neither was ever needed for the answer."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: about 4 min (d1), about 30 s (d4) and about 2.3 min","-  (d6). `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If the decoded asset already matches the answer_format, submit it.","-- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15): sets can come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.","-  A solver that branched on the day's codec name would have failed 4/5 sets. Decode each APK on its own.","+- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: ~4 min (d1), ~30 s (d4), ~2.3 min (d6).","+  `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If a static value matches the answer_format, submit it.","+- **Taking `data` at face value** (d20): `data` was an entry path, not a value. Never submit or \"decode\" a string that","+  names a zip entry; open the entry. Always fullmatch the ANS regex on the final value.","+- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15+): sets come from older days with different codecs and extra entries."," - **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15-d16): the `.so` is ~14 KB, unstripped, the answer a literal. Use","-  `strings`/`nm` first, then `objdump -d` of the one `Java_*` export (d16 gate = 0x30 bytes). Ghidra is overkill.","+  `strings`/`nm`, then `objdump -d` of the one `Java_*` export. Same for d20's payload: `strings` before `jadx`."," - **Trusting the question's case ref in Mastery** (d16): it can name a different day/case than the APK it points at.","-- **New codec, generic solver silent** (d17 `indexed`): the race probe produced nothing, costing ~20 s before a worker","-  added the decoder (lib now has the generic int-list permutation, but the next unseen codec will repeat this). When the puzzle JSON has an unknown codec, write the 5-line decoder straight away (anchor on","-  `ANS-`); do not wait on lib or decompile anything.","-- **Trusting dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` strings** (d17-d18 TT): the TT dex had neither. Key the decoder on the JSON's own fields.","-- **split/indexed order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate the candidates against the answer regex","-  instead of guessing.","-- **caesar codec:** the shift is over raw codepoints, not the alphabet (`data` contains `]`, `` ` ``, `<`, `>` --","-  JSON-escaped as `<`/`>`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that","-  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`.","+- **New codec, generic solver silent** (d17 `indexed`, ~20 s lost): when the JSON has an unknown codec, write the","+  5-line decoder straight away (anchor on `ANS-`); do not wait on lib or decompile anything.","+- **Trusting dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` strings** (d17-d20 TT): the TT dex drops the tag. Key the decoder on the JSON's fields.","+- **split/indexed order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate against the answer regex instead of guessing.","+- **caesar codec:** shift over raw codepoints, not the alphabet; json-load (escapes `<`/`>`), never regex the raw text."," - **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.","-- **6-11 s timed windows** (d2-d9) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1 s, so do no","-  decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly (the solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess).","+- **Short timed windows** are dominated by start + download + submit; solve is <1 s. No decompiling in-window: the","+  solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess."," - **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove","-  server-side impact\", d13 \"app-controlled wrapping key\", d14 \"seeded nonces\", d15 \"split configuration from DEX and a","-  native library\", d16 \"type or length assumption that changes backend authorization\", d18 \"recover only the strings","-  that reach security-sensitive APIs\", d19 \"reconstruct reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs\"):","-  judge by what the APK contains (pcap/HAR, token file, `.db`, cert, network config, native lib, `Random`/`Cipher`/KDF/","-  `forName`/`getDeclaredMethod` refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.","-- **Hand-typed codec tables:** use `lib.android.puzzle_candidates`/`decode_payload` so a missed branch can't cost a","-  timed run.","+  server-side impact\", d15 \"split configuration\", d16 \"type or length assumption\", d18 \"strings that reach","+  security-sensitive APIs\", d19 \"reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs\", d20 \"challenge-signed","+  secondary DEX ... module contract\"): judge by what the APK contains (extra entries, `Random`/`Cipher`/`forName`/","+  `DexClassLoader`/`MessageDigest` refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb."," - **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json`; check `hctf status` before re-solving.","-- Watch for the cheap escalation (not yet seen in 19 days): answer only in the dex, `strings.xml`, BuildConfig or the","-  `.so`, or computed by code. The TT builds keep previewing it: d16 a gated `Java_*` export, d17 a renamed `b -> a` chain","-  with decoys, d18 a per-byte `decryptByte`, d19 a reflective `dispatch`. If several `ANS-` candidates ever appear, take","-  the one that flows into `proof=` (`proof_flow_scan`), never the first regex hit; for reflection, resolve the","-  class/method NAMES first (`reflection_scan`: names may be xor/Base64/reversed strings or come from a dispatch map keyed","-  by a deep-link/extra value), then evaluate only the target that is actually invoked. Derive keys/params from code or","-  the known `ANS-` prefix; never guess.","+- **Escalation watch:** d20 moved the answer one hop (JSON -> nested dex). Next cheap steps: the payload encrypted /","+  XOR'd / zipped (unwrap by magic known plaintext, key from host dex), several payloads where only the one whose digest","+  matches a pinned hash (\"challenge-signed\") is loaded, >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host naming the real field/","+  method (`moduleContract`), class shadowing between host and payload, or a stage-2 loader. If several candidates","+  appear, take the one the code actually returns into `proof=` (`proof_flow_scan`), never the first regex hit."]}],"originalFile":"# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture: `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`, `classes.dex`,\n  `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF` (6 entries). Extras: d10 `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` +\n  `resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, ~12.8 KB). One question, `answer` = `ANS-` +\n  16 uppercase hex.\n- Each day has a new Android IPC/security THEME, written in the manifest `<meta-data android:name=\"huntress.mechanic\">`\n  and in a dex string `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable\n  PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider, JS-interface origin trust, cleartext session, permissive X509\n  trust manager, NSC exception, SharedPreferences credential, client-side SQLite authz, app-controlled Keystore key,\n  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` \"challenge-owned JNI shared library\" d15, `jni_length` \"Java-to-native validation\n  mismatch\" d16, `identifier_obfuscation` \"R8-style identifier collapse\" d17, `string_decryption` \"runtime string\n  decryption\" d18, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\" d19). The theme was flavour only: no day required\n  exploiting it, even with a matching stub class (`WebViewBridge`, `TrustEveryone`, `PredictableCrypto`,\n  `NativeLibrarySecrets`, `JNIBoundary`, `EncryptedStrings`, `ReflectionMaze`) or a prompt demanding a live action. d16 is the first day whose TT/Mastery build had a REAL gate in code (a JNI export guarding the answer),\n  yet the answer was still a literal in the asset and in `.rodata`.\n- What varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split, hex,\n  caesar+key, then repeats; d15-d16 `native`, whose `data` is already the plaintext answer; d17 `indexed` = permutation\n  `data` + `order[]`; d18 back to `xor`, its 3rd day after d4/d11 -- old codecs recur on new themes; d19 `reflection`,\n  a theme-named codec whose `data` is already the plaintext, like `native`). The dex also holds\n  the codec name next to a `CODEC` string constant. Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day:\n  decode it from the first 4 chars, which must become `ANS-`.\n- **Since d15 Mastery is a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets are APKs from earlier days plus one of today's (d15: d01 plain,\n  d07 caesar, d10 split, d14 caesar, d15 native; d16: d01 plain, d04 xor, d11 xor, d13 base64, d16 native; d17: d04 xor,\n  d08 reverse, d12 hex, d14 caesar, d17 indexed; d18: d03 base64, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d18 xor; d19: d03\n  base64, d05 split, d11 xor, d18 xor, d19 reflection), all under\n  today's prompt text. Solve each set from its own puzzle JSON, never from \"today's codec\".\n- In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?\n  case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM\n  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 19 days.\n- Escalation watch: d15 shipped the first native lib and d16 the first native GATE (`Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence\n  (env, cls, int len)` returns `arena_value` only if `huntress_arena_length_accepts(len, 0)`: `len > 0xffff &&\n  (uint16)len == 0`, i.e. 65536). The answer was STILL in the asset and in `.rodata`. If a later day drops it from the\n  asset, read the gate statically and take the value it returns (`lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain).\n- Pattern d16-d19: the SINGLE variant carries only flavour; the TT build carries the real mechanic in code (d16 JNI gate,\n  d17 renamed class `a` + dex hint `R8-style collapse: follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy`/`telemetry` strings,\n  d18 a `decryptByte` method + `STRUCTURAL` string in class `EncryptedStrings`, d19 only `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings\n  -- no `forName`/`getMethod`/`invoke` anywhere). Every time the asset STILL held the answer.\n  Read the TT/Mastery APK's dex strings when you reverse a day, not just the single's.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44, d16 Mastery\n  d04-set 21, d11-set 232, d17 d04-set 104, d18: 20/99/233, d19 Mastery d11-set 109, d18-set 44 -- full 0-255 range, so never assume printable keys; caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4, d14: 9/10/17,4,7, d15 Mastery d07-set 15, d14-set 4) and split/offset parameters re-roll per variant:\n  read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs (`reverse`, `base64`, `native`, `reflection`) differ\n  only in `data`. Theme-named codecs (`native` d15-d16, `reflection` d19) carried the PLAINTEXT in `data` in every variant.\n  d17 `indexed`: `order[]` was the SAME list in single, TT and the Mastery d17 set (`order[i] = (3 + 7*i) mod 20`), only\n  `data` changed -- still read it from the JSON, a later day may re-roll it.\n  Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`, else `decode_any`; unknown name -> known-plaintext\n  `ANS-` trick; any int-list field of len(data) -> try scatter and gather, keep the regex match.\n- **Mastery set mix (NEW d15)** -- sets can be fixtures of DIFFERENT days (codec, theme, package `dNN`, extra entries\n  like `res/xml/...` or `lib/x86_64/*.so` all differ per set; the puzzle JSON `day` field and dex `DAY-NN:` tag name the\n  source day). The day picks re-roll per attempt (d15: 01/07/10/14/15 vs 03/07/09/13/15; d16: 01/04/11/13/16; d17:\n  04/08/12/14/17, while the pre-start `status` preview listed MOB-02/06/09 -- re-dealt at start; d18: preview MOB-01/06/\n  10/15/18, dealt 03/07/12/13/18; d19: 03/05/11/18/19, d05 split as a 6-entry APK, `order` [2,0,1]); the last set was\n  always today's. Today's Mastery set has its own manifest label\n  (`Day 18 Mastery | concept Day 18: Encrypted Strings`, manifest 3540 B vs 3492 B) -- cosmetic. d16: the QUESTION's case ref/package (`MOB-06-..`, `d08`, `d14`) did NOT match the APK's own\n  (`MOB-04`, `d11`, `d13`), so the contract text does not predict the codec either.\n  Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding (`puzzle_candidates` over each APK) -- never branch on the day or case ref.\n- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref `MOB-NN-<10 hex>`, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback\n  attempt slug change per variant. None of these feed the answer.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. Set count varies: 3 sets\n  (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5 sets (d8, d9, d15, d16). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3.\n- **Dex decoy/hint strings (d17-d18)** -- single dex: `CODEC`, `CONTROL`, `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>` tag, `describe`; TT\n  and today's Mastery set: NO `DAY-NN` tag and no `describe`, instead the mechanic in code -- d17 `R8-style collapse:\n  follow b -> a and ignore field c`, `decoy`, `telemetry`, `authorization` (2672 B vs 2588 B); d18 `decryptByte`,\n  `STRUCTURAL`, the mechanic name as a bare string (2628 B vs 2588 B); d19 `dispatch`, `STRUCTURAL`, the mechanic string,\n  `CODEC` kept (2656 B vs 2596 B), still no reflection API. Rule: never require the dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN`\n  strings to find or decode the puzzle; a TT-only method name (`decryptByte`) is the cue to what the next escalation\n  computes in code.\n- **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON (d15-d16: also duplicated in the `.so` `.rodata`); if it decodes\n  to nothing, fall back to dex/resources/native (`raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`).\n- **Native lib shape (NEW d16)** -- same day, different `.so` builds: the single variant shipped the d15-style 13648 B lib\n  (exports `huntress_arena_secret`/`huntress_arena_day` only, dex 2584 B, no `loadLibrary`); TT and the Mastery d16 set\n  shipped a 14128 B lib adding `huntress_arena_length_accepts` + `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence` (dex 2760 B with\n  `System.loadLibrary(\"arena\")`, `nativeEvidence`, and a description string \"Java int length narrows to an unsigned\n  native 16-bit boundary before authorization\"). Rule: never key on export names or lib size; take the asset value,\n  cross-check `ANS-` literals in the `.so`; if none, follow the `Java_*` export to the pointer it returns.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (held the answer all 19 days). triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` and prints the JSON |\n| puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (table below). Check the result fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before you submit |\n| puzzle JSON with an int list next to `data` (d17 `indexed`: `data` 20 chars + `order[20]`) | `order[i]` is the OUTPUT slot of `data[i]` (scatter, same as `split`): `r[order[i]] = data[i]`. Tell: `data` holds `A`,`N`,`S`,`-` at the positions where `order` has 0,1,2,3 |\n| Codec name not in the table (d7 `caesar`, d15 `native`, d17 `indexed`, d19 `reflection`) | first check whether `data` already matches `ANS-` (d15, d19: a codec named after the theme was plaintext). Else compare `data[:4]` with `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key |\n| `lib/<abi>/*.so` in the APK (d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`, 13.6-14.1 KB, not stripped) | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` and `nm -D --defined-only` first (d15: exports `huntress_arena_secret`/`huntress_arena_day`, 0x20-byte `.text`, answer as a literal in `.rodata`). Only if the answer is not a literal, route to binary-re (rizin / pyelftools + capstone, or the JNI `Java_*` export) |\n| Native GATE (d16: `Java_*_nativeEvidence(int)` -> `*_length_accepts`; \"type or length assumption\") | the gate only decides whether the export returns `arena_value`; that pointer is the `.rodata` `ANS-` literal. If a question ever asks for the bypass input: `objdump -d --no-show-raw-insn f.so` the checker (d16: `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -> 65536) |\n| \"Recover split configuration from DEX and a native library\" (d15) | the \"split\" was narrative: the asset `data` and the `.so` string were the SAME full answer, and the dex held only `CODEC`/`native`/`CONTROL`. Cross-check the two, submit |\n| No puzzle JSON, or it decodes to no `ANS-` | `lib.android.extract_answer` (zip scan, then dex strings incl. multidex, then apktool/jadx scan), then `strings -a classes*.dex lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |\n| Need the theme, component, scheme or exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` (fast). `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`. Also `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |\n| 1-letter classes `<pkg>/a`, `b`; dex hint \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\", strings `decoy`/`telemetry` (d17 R8 theme) | first check the asset (it still held the answer d17). If the answer ever leaves it: `jadx --deobf -d w/jadx x.apk`, follow the chain the hint names, ignore the named decoy field; prefer the value that flows into `proof=` |\n| String-encryption theme: class `EncryptedStrings`, dex method `decryptByte`, mechanic `runtime string decryption` (d18) | asset first (d18: `xor` codec, answer there). If the answer ever leaves it: `lib.android.dex_eval_scan` (mini Dalvik evaluator; note it feeds params `\"\"`/0, so a helper called with constant args needs those args from the call site) and `jadx` the helper; re-implement the per-byte loop in python, anchor on `ANS-` |\n| Reflection theme: class `ReflectionMaze`, mechanic `reflective secret dispatch`, TT strings `dispatch`/`STRUCTURAL` (d19) | asset first (d19: answer in `data`). If it ever leaves: `lib.android.reflection_scan(apk)` (runs the methods that call `getDeclaredMethod`/`Field.get`, resolving encoded names), then `proof_flow_scan` to pick the value that reaches `proof=` |\n| Need handler logic (URL built, extras read, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, then `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; whole app: `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |\n| Need resources or strings.xml / smali | `apktool d -f -o work/apktool x.apk` |\n| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it. It is device-local (refused on Homebase, times out elsewhere). The answer is static |\n| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session against the backend\" d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9) | still static: check `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/network config first; none shipped. Decode the asset, submit |\n| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen yet) | Android backup = 24-byte header + zlib stream: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` (or abe.jar) |\n| Mastery artifact names like `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the `delivery N: ` prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact` does this). Ids are `setN.answer`; each set may be a different day's fixture (d15) |\n\nPuzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):\n- `plain`: data is the answer. `native` (d15-d16): same, duplicated in `lib/x86_64/libarena.so`. `reflection` (d19): same.\n- `reverse`: reverse the string (`...-SNA` -> `ANS-...`).\n- `base64` (d3, d9, d13): `base64 -d` (`QU5TLTNEM0I4MDM5NTI0MEI4RUU=` -> `ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`).\n- `hex` (d6, d12): `xxd -r -p`.\n- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`. Plain ASCII codepoint shift: `chr(ord(c) - key)` for EVERY char (digits and `-`\n  shift too, e.g. `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`). A letters-only mod-26 ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.\n- `xor` (d4, d11, d18): data is base64. b64-decode, then XOR every byte with the int `key` (0-255, re-rolled per variant;\n  lib also accepts a numeric-string or repeating string key).\n- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, where `order[i]` is the OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]` (not `parts[order[i]]`).\n  Try both readings and keep the one that fullmatches `ANS-`.\n- `indexed` (d17): `{data: 20 chars, order: [20 ints]}`, per-CHARACTER permutation with the same semantics:\n  `r[order[i]] = data[i]` (`-2FE1A2D163AA1N51SC0` + `[3,10,17,4,...]` -> `ANS-E26A5C21D3110FA1`). Built into lib after\n  d17: `lib.android.permutation_candidates(p)` tries scatter + gather over ANY int-list field of len(data) (also\n  `perm*`/`shuffle*`/unknown codecs), and `transposition_candidates(s)` covers keyless stride/rail-fence shuffles.\n- `lib.android.decode_payload` covers every codec above, `puzzle_candidates(apk)` also does split/indexed (both order readings),\n  and `decode_any` is the name-agnostic fallback (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`). Call them instead of re-typing a\n  table. Unknown codec + int key: `key_or_shift = f(data[:4], \"ANS-\")` (xor: byte ^; shift: ord diff).\n- Code-side scanners prebuilt after d17 (for when the answer leaves the asset): `renamed_chain_scan` (follow R8 `b -> a`\n  chains, hint-aware), `proof_flow_scan` (rank `ANS-` candidates by what reaches `proof=`), `dex_eval_scan` (mini Dalvik\n  evaluator for xor/char-array builders), `reflection_scan`, `mapping_restore_scan`, `signing_block_scan`,\n  `zip_structure_scan`, `integrity_key_scan`. `extract_answer(apk)` chains only the entry/dex/nested/cipher/cert/integrity\n  stages -- call the chain/proof/eval/reflection scanners yourself.\n\n## Day by day\n\n**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, one codec per day, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (CORRECT ~5.4 min,\n~4 min lost probing `127.0.0.1:19090` via `hctf hb exec curl`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s; Mastery expired 8x\nin a 6 s window until Homebase prewarm); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay `xor` key per\nvariant 103/189/31/81 (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot of `parts[i]` (27 s; TT/Mastery 7 s\nwindow, solve 0.08 s of 5.3 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (exported provider with a null `query()` stub; ~3 min, 2.3 min\nlost on the loopback).\n\n**Days 7-15** (same fixture; theme stubs never needed; all 0 wrong, TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window): d7 WebView Bridge,\nnew `caesar` key 10, spotted by eye (`K`-10=`A`), 52 s; d8 Cleartext Session `reverse` (no traffic shipped); d9 Trust\nEveryone `base64`; d10 Network Config Split `split` (8-entry fixture + NSC, still static); d11 Local Secrets `xor` key 81\n(dex `client_secret` a decoy); d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`; d14 Predictable Crypto\n`caesar` key 9 (raw JSON escapes `\\\\`/`<` -- json-load it). d12+ solved in ~3-5 s by the carried-over solver. d15 Native\nLibrary Secrets (`jni_secret`): first `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13648 B, answer literal in `.rodata`), codec `native` =\nplaintext answer = the `.so` string (\"split\" was narrative). First MIXED-DAY Mastery (d01/07/10/14/15).\n\n**Days 16-18** (fixture unchanged; asset held the answer every time; 0 wrong): d16 JNI Boundary (`jni_length`), codec\n`native`; TT/Mastery `.so` added `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int len)` -> `huntress_arena_length_accepts`\n(`len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` = 65536) returning the `.rodata` literal; probe ~7 s, TT 5.3 s, Mastery 5.5 s. d17 Name\nCollapse (`identifier_obfuscation`): renamed class `<pkg>/a`, NEW codec `indexed` (`r[order[i]] = data[i]`, same `order` in\nall variants); TT dex hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy`/`telemetry`. Race probe FAILED (no decoder), duel\nworker added `_indexed` -> CORRECT ~24.5 s. d18 Encrypted Strings (`string_decryption`): codec `xor` (3rd time, b64 + int\nkey); single dex had no cipher code, TT/Mastery added `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`; carried-over solver\nCORRECT ~5.2 s after start, TT 2.42 s, Mastery 5.05 s in-window. Lesson: the title names the theme; the codec decides.\n\n**Day 19 — Reflection Maze** (manifest `huntress.mechanic`=`reflective secret dispatch`, dex\n`DAY-19:reflective_dispatch:reflective secret dispatch`, class `ReflectionMaze`, deep link `huntress19://reflection-maze/\nunlock`; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs.\"; dex blurb \"cross the\nreflective secret dispatch boundary\")\n- Artifact: the 6-entry fixture (APK 12704 B, dex 2596 B, no `.so`/arsc); classes `MainActivity`, `ChallengeActivity`,\n  `ReflectionMaze`. NEW codec name `reflection`, but `{\"codec\":\"reflection\",\"data\":\"ANS-<16 hex>\"}` -- `data` was already\n  the answer (same shape as `native`). No dex in any variant held `forName`/`getDeclaredMethod`/`invoke`: there was no\n  reflective dispatch to reconstruct and no \"equivalent call graphs\" -- one class, one value.\n- TT + today's Mastery set: dex 2656 B, `DAY-19` tag and `describe` dropped, `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` added (`CODEC`\n  kept). Same TT-only-hint pattern as d17-d18, still unused for the answer.\n- Key insight / tools: none needed beyond the carried-over solver: `puzzle_candidates` returns `data` when it already\n  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`, whatever the codec name. Unknown codec name -> regex-check `data` before decoding.\n- Time: race probe submitted from the solver -> CORRECT 1.9 s probe, ~3.2 s after start (13:00:07.3Z -> 13:00:10.5Z), no\n  LLM turn. TT in-window 1.88 s (solve 0.2 s); Mastery 5 sets (d03 base64, d05 split, d11 xor, d18 xor, d19 reflection)\n  in-window 1.34 s (solve 0.06 s). All first try, 0 wrong. GM spelling: same `answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 or 5 sets), one APK per set.\n- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding, no whitespace.\n- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-19). The GM accepts the decoded\n  `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend\n  answer code returned for this case\".\n- Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An\n  empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.\n- Prompt boilerplate repeats daily: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In a mixed\n  Mastery bundle the prompt text is today's; on d15 each set's `NN` named its source day, but on d16 the question's case\n  ref/package did not match the APK's own (MOB-06 question -> a d04 APK). Neither was ever needed for the answer.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: about 4 min (d1), about 30 s (d4) and about 2.3 min\n  (d6). `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If the decoded asset already matches the answer_format, submit it.\n- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15): sets can come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.\n  A solver that branched on the day's codec name would have failed 4/5 sets. Decode each APK on its own.\n- **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15-d16): the `.so` is ~14 KB, unstripped, the answer a literal. Use\n  `strings`/`nm` first, then `objdump -d` of the one `Java_*` export (d16 gate = 0x30 bytes). Ghidra is overkill.\n- **Trusting the question's case ref in Mastery** (d16): it can name a different day/case than the APK it points at.\n- **New codec, generic solver silent** (d17 `indexed`): the race probe produced nothing, costing ~20 s before a worker\n  added the decoder (lib now has the generic int-list permutation, but the next unseen codec will repeat this). When the puzzle JSON has an unknown codec, write the 5-line decoder straight away (anchor on\n  `ANS-`); do not wait on lib or decompile anything.\n- **Trusting dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` strings** (d17-d18 TT): the TT dex had neither. Key the decoder on the JSON's own fields.\n- **split/indexed order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate the candidates against the answer regex\n  instead of guessing.\n- **caesar codec:** the shift is over raw codepoints, not the alphabet (`data` contains `]`, `` ` ``, `<`, `>` --\n  JSON-escaped as `<`/`>`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that\n  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`.\n- **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.\n- **6-11 s timed windows** (d2-d9) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1 s, so do no\n  decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly (the solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess).\n- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove\n  server-side impact\", d13 \"app-controlled wrapping key\", d14 \"seeded nonces\", d15 \"split configuration from DEX and a\n  native library\", d16 \"type or length assumption that changes backend authorization\", d18 \"recover only the strings\n  that reach security-sensitive APIs\", d19 \"reconstruct reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs\"):\n  judge by what the APK contains (pcap/HAR, token file, `.db`, cert, network config, native lib, `Random`/`Cipher`/KDF/\n  `forName`/`getDeclaredMethod` refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.\n- **Hand-typed codec tables:** use `lib.android.puzzle_candidates`/`decode_payload` so a missed branch can't cost a\n  timed run.\n- **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json`; check `hctf status` before re-solving.\n- Watch for the cheap escalation (not yet seen in 19 days): answer only in the dex, `strings.xml`, BuildConfig or the\n  `.so`, or computed by code. The TT builds keep previewing it: d16 a gated `Java_*` export, d17 a renamed `b -> a` chain\n  with decoys, d18 a per-byte `decryptByte`, d19 a reflective `dispatch`. If several `ANS-` candidates ever appear, take\n  the one that flows into `proof=` (`proof_flow_scan`), never the first regex hit; for reflection, resolve the\n  class/method NAMES first (`reflection_scan`: names may be xor/Base64/reversed strings or come from a dispatch map keyed\n  by a deep-link/extra value), then evaluate only the target that is actually invoked. Derive keys/params from code or\n  the known `ANS-` prefix; never guess.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RrbYPxjaYVtP47VjhULThJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
