ver the wrapper from the expected file magic\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Next step after D20's plain payload: the asset dex/jar/so XOR'd, added, reversed, base64/hex-text, gzip/zlib/lzma, or AES with a host-dex key. Generic unwrapper: for each asset without a known magic, try known-plaintext headers (`dex\\\\n035\\\\0`..`dex\\\\n041\\\\0`, `cdex001\\\\0`, `PK\\\\x03\\\\x04`, `\\\\x7fELF\\\\x02\\\\x01\\\\x01`, `SQLite format 3\\\\0`) to derive single-byte, repeating (1-16 B, period found by consistency), add/sub and rolling (`k+i`, `k^i`) keys; verify by a full dex header check (file_size field == len, adler32 valid) or a zip central directory; also try text layers (base64/hex/reversed) and compressors first. asset-cipher-dex-loader covers AES with an explicit key -- reuse it, then recurse the decoded bytes through puzzle-entry-pointer-follow.\"},\n {\"id\":\"multi-stage-loader-recurse\",\"concept\":\"stage-1 payload loads/decrypts stage-2 (row 85)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Loaded later' can chain: stage-1 dex (from assets) references another entry name + key (const-string, fill-array-data) and decrypts it into stage-2 (dex, jar, zip with classes.dex, .so via System.load). After unwrapping stage 1, scan ITS strings for entry names present in the outer APK or in nested containers and for key material, feed them to payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap / static-key-cipher-decode, recurse to depth 4 with a byte budget. Report the stage path with each candidate.\"},\n {\"id\":\"classloader-shadow-resolve\",\"concept\":\"same class descriptor in host and payload dex; delegation order decides (row 84)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Index classes across classes*.dex and every payload dex; when a descriptor appears in more than one, decide which definition runs: DexClassLoader/PathClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader are parent-first (host/boot copy wins) unless the app defines a ClassLoader subclass overriding loadClass/findClass (child-first) or loads via a fresh loader with a null/boot parent (const/4 null passed as parent). Evaluate only the winning definition's members; demote ANS- candidates from shadowed copies.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cdex-vdex-string-pool\",\"concept\":\"compact/optimised dex payloads (cdex001, vdex, oat) (row 86)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If a payload is CompactDex (`cdex001`) or wrapped in vdex (`vdex0xx`, holds dex/cdex sections) or an OAT ELF (`oatdata` symbol), androguard and dex_strings fail. Pure python: parse vdex section headers to extract embedded dex/cdex; for cdex, read header string_ids (offsets are relative to data_off) and decode MUTF-8 strings; for oat, locate embedded dex via `oatdata` + OatDexFile entries or by scanning for `dex\\\\n0`/`cdex` magic. Feed strings to the ANS regex and to module-contract-member-eval where possible.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-payload-system-load\",\"concept\":\"native code loaded later: `System.load(<extracted asset .so>)` instead of lib/<abi>/\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Native twin of D20: an ELF stored under assets/ (or inside the payload dex's raw resources), possibly xor/zlib-wrapped, extracted to filesDir and loaded with System.load. Detect ELF magic in any entry (after payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap) and run the existing native chain on it (strings/.rodata, jni-export-return-trace, registernatives-table, native-so-emulate-export, native-init-array-decrypt) as if it were lib/x86_64/*.so; also handle an arm64-only payload via multi-abi-arm-native.\"},\n {\"id\":\"attestation-jws-claims\",\"concept\":\"Play Integrity / SafetyNet attestation token shipped in the app (row 87)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"MASVS-RESILIENCE leftover after loader/integrity days. Find 3-part `eyJ...` JWS strings in dex/assets/JSON; b64url-decode header + payload; report claims (nonce, apkPackageName, apkCertificateDigestSha256, ctsProfil