pointers.\"},\n {\"id\":\"module-contract-member-eval\",\"concept\":\"secondary-dex 'module contract': value of the host-named class/field/method in the payload (D20 TT `moduleContract`)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D20 TT host dex added `moduleContract` and `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`; the payload had strings `ANSWER`/`CONTRACT`. When a payload holds >1 ANS- candidate the target member decides. Pure python over the payload dex (androguard or own parser): map static final fields to values (class_def static_values encoded_array + sput in <clinit>), map each method returning String to its const-string/StringBuilder result via dex_eval_scan; resolve the target from host strings (`<entry>:<Class>`, method names near `loadClass`/`getMethod`/`moduleContract`, interface method names implemented by the payload class, fields named ANSWER/CONTRACT/answer). Rank: host-named member > field named ANSWER/CONTRACT > interface impl reachable from host > others (demoted).\"},\n {\"id\":\"payload-digest-pinned-select\",\"concept\":\"'challenge-signed' secondary module: several payloads, the pinned digest/signature picks the loaded one (row 83)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D20 prompt said 'challenge-signed' but shipped no verify code; the obvious next twist is N payloads (payload_a.dex, payload_b.dex, *.bin) or a decoy module. Compute for every non-META entry: SHA-256/SHA-1/MD5/CRC32 (hex upper/lower + base64 + base64url), dex header adler32/sha1 fields, the v1 MANIFEST.MF/.SF per-entry digests; collect host-dex constants (64/40/32-hex, 44-char base64, ints) and sidecar entries (`*.sig`, `*.sha256`, `*.digest`, JSON fields `sha256`/`digest`/`signature`). Select the payload whose digest matches a host/sidecar pin (also check MANIFEST.MF digest validity to reject a tampered decoy), run the candidate chain on it first, demote the rest. If a PKCS#1/Ed25519 signature + public key are shipped, verify with pycryptodome.\"},\n {\"id\":\"payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap\",\"concept\":\"encrypted/wrapped secondary payload: recover the wrapper from the expected file magic\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Next step after D20's plain payload: the asset dex/jar/so XOR'd, added, reversed, base64/hex-text, gzip/zlib/lzma, or AES with a host-dex key. Generic unwrapper: for each asset without a known magic, try known-plaintext headers (`dex\\\\n035\\\\0`..`dex\\\\n041\\\\0`, `cdex001\\\\0`, `PK\\\\x03\\\\x04`, `\\\\x7fELF\\\\x02\\\\x01\\\\x01`, `SQLite format 3\\\\0`) to derive single-byte, repeating (1-16 B, period found by consistency), add/sub and rolling (`k+i`, `k^i`) keys; verify by a full dex header check (file_size field == len, adler32 valid) or a zip central directory; also try text layers (base64/hex/reversed) and compressors first. asset-cipher-dex-loader covers AES with an explicit key -- reuse it, then recurse the decoded bytes through puzzle-entry-pointer-follow.\"},\n {\"id\":\"multi-stage-loader-recurse\",\"concept\":\"stage-1 payload loads/decrypts stage-2 (row 85)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Loaded later' can chain: stage-1 dex (from assets) references another entry name + key (const-string, fill-array-data) and decrypts it into stage-2 (dex, jar, zip with classes.dex, .so via System.load). After unwrapping stage 1, scan ITS strings for entry names present in the outer APK or in nested containers and for key material, feed them to payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap / static-key-cipher-decode, recurse to depth 4 with a byte budget. Report the stage path with each candidate.\"},\n {\"id\":\"classloader-shadow-resolve\",\"concept\":\"same class descriptor in host and payload dex; delegation order decides (row 84)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Index classes across classes*.dex and every payload dex; when a descriptor appears in more than one, decide which definition runs: DexClassLoader/PathClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader are parent-first (host/boot copy wins) unless the app defines a ClassLoader subclass overriding loadClass/findClass (child-first) or loads via a fresh loader with a null/boot parent (const/4 null passed as parent). Evaluate only the winning definition's members; demote ANS- candidates from shadowed copies.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cdex-vdex-string-pool\",\"concept\":\"compact/optimised dex payloads (cdex001, vdex, oat) (row 86)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If a payload is CompactDex (`cdex001`) or wrapped in vdex (`vdex0xx`, holds dex/cdex sections) or an OAT ELF (`oatdata` symbol), androguard and dex_strings fail. Pure python: parse vdex section headers to extract embedded dex/cdex; for cdex, read header string_ids (offsets are relative to data_off) and decode MUTF-8 strings; for oat, locate embedded dex via `oatdata` + OatDexFile entries or by scanning for `dex\\\\n0`/`cdex` magic. Feed strings to the ANS regex and to module-contract-member-eval where possible.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-payload-system-load\",\"concept\":\"native code loaded later: `System.load(<extracted asset .so>)` instead of lib/<abi>/\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Native twin of D20: an ELF stored under assets/ (or inside the payload dex's raw resources), possibly xor/zlib-wrapped, extracted to filesDir and loaded with System.load. Detect ELF magic in any entry (after payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap) and run the existing native chain on it (strings/.rodata, jni-export-return-trace, registernatives-table, native-so-emulate-export, native-init-array-decrypt) as if it were lib/x86_64/*.so; also handle an arm64-only payload via multi-abi-arm-native.\"},\n {\"id\":\"attestation-jws-claims\",\"concept\":\"Play Integrity / SafetyNet attestation token shipped in the app (row 87)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"MASVS-RESILIENCE leftover after loader/integrity days. Find 3-part `eyJ...` JWS strings in dex/assets/JSON; b64url-decode header + payload; report claims (nonce, apkPackageName, apkCertificateDigestSha256, ctsProfileMatch/basicIntegrity, requestDetails/appIntegrity/deviceIntegrity verdicts, tokenPayloadExternal). Compare the cert digest claim with the APK's signing cert (cert-and-signing-facts) and the package name; if the answer is derived (HMAC of nonce, verdict-gated branch), hand the claim values to dex-gated-branch-consts / messagedigest-derived-answer. Verify x5c chain/signature with pycryptodome when a cert is embedded.\"},\n {\"id\":\"xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack\",\"concept\":\"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ lz4 (row 55)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure python so no pyxamstore is needed in-window: XALZ per-assembly (magic `XALZ`, u32 descriptor index, u32 uncompressed size, lz4.block payload), assemblies.blob `XABA` (header, assembly descriptors with data offset/size, optional hash tables) and .NET 8 `libassemblies.<abi>.blob.so` (payload in an ELF section `payload`). Output each DLL; scan its #US user-string heap (UTF-16) for ANS- via the existing utf16 pool scan.\"}\n]\ngaps=new[:4]+[g for g in rest if g['action']=='note']+new[4:]+[g for g in rest if g['action']!='note']\njs='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+'\\n]'\ns=s[:i+8]+js+s[j+1:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read()\ni=s.index('```json\\n'); j=s.index('\\n```',i+8)\ng=json.loads(s[i+8:j]); print(len(g), sum(1 for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild'), [x['id'] for x in g])\nc=s.index('## Recognition cues'); d=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nprint('cue lines', s[c:d].count('\\n'))\nEOF"}}}
